2768, "start": 127.68, "end": 132.78, "text": " And you are going to look at every system in your life completely differently after this.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 291, 366, 516, 281, 574, 412, 633, 1185, 294, 428, 993, 2584, 7614, 934, 341, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 12768, "start": 132.9, "end": 133.46, "text": " Oh, guaranteed.", "tokens": [50626, 876, 11, 18031, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 12768, "start": 133.8, "end": 138.22, "text": " Because before we can even talk about how a system survives or how it breaks,", "tokens": [50671, 1436, 949, 321, 393, 754, 751, 466, 577, 257, 1185, 46231, 420, 577, 309, 9857, 11, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 12768, "start": 138.64000000000001, "end": 141.94, "text": " Flixson argues we have to define what a system can actually see.", "tokens": [50913, 3235, 970, 3015, 38218, 321, 362, 281, 6964, 437, 257, 1185, 393, 767, 536, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 12768, "start": 142.18, "end": 142.44, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51090, 1079, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 12768, "start": 142.88, "end": 146.66, "text": " We have to start at the foundational level of what the text calls distinctions.", "tokens": [51125, 492, 362, 281, 722, 412, 264, 32195, 1496, 295, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 1483, 49798, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 12768, "start": 147.26000000000002, "end": 151.96, "text": " So the premise here is that a system is not defined by the physical objects it contains.", "tokens": [51344, 407, 264, 22045, 510, 307, 300, 257, 1185, 307, 406, 7642, 538, 264, 4001, 6565, 309, 8306, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 12768, "start": 152.28, "end": 155.52, "text": " It is defined solely by the distinctions it can express.", "tokens": [51595, 467, 307, 7642, 23309, 538, 264, 1483, 49798, 309, 393, 5109, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 12768, "start": 155.94, "end": 156.18, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51778, 1033, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12467767371505988, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553502496351568e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15618, "start": 156.18, "end": 159.92000000000002, "text": " The text introduces this concept of the distinguishability space,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 31472, 341, 3410, 295, 264, 20206, 2310, 1901, 11, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 15618, "start": 160.14000000000001, "end": 165.76000000000002, "text": " which, you know, mathematically is a set of objects and an equivalence relation on those objects.", "tokens": [50563, 597, 11, 291, 458, 11, 44003, 307, 257, 992, 295, 6565, 293, 364, 9052, 655, 9721, 322, 729, 6565, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 15618, "start": 166.02, "end": 167.76000000000002, "text": " Right. But let's break that down for people.", "tokens": [50857, 1779, 13, 583, 718, 311, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 561, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 15618, "start": 167.96, "end": 170.5, "text": " Sure. In plain terms, imagine you are a system.", "tokens": [50954, 4894, 13, 682, 11121, 2115, 11, 3811, 291, 366, 257, 1185, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 15618, "start": 170.9, "end": 173.48000000000002, "text": " The universe contains an infinite amount of detail.", "tokens": [51101, 440, 6445, 8306, 364, 13785, 2372, 295, 2607, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 15618, "start": 173.9, "end": 177.5, "text": " If two states of the universe look exactly the same to your sensors,", "tokens": [51251, 759, 732, 4368, 295, 264, 6445, 574, 2293, 264, 912, 281, 428, 14840, 11, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 15618, "start": 178.16, "end": 182.82, "text": " then for all practical purposes within your reality, they are the exact same state.", "tokens": [51464, 550, 337, 439, 8496, 9932, 1951, 428, 4103, 11, 436, 366, 264, 1900, 912, 1785, 13, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12243008394853784, "compression_ratio": 1.6118881118881119, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881603536952894e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 18282, "start": 182.82, "end": 189.23999999999998, "text": " Okay. Let's unpack this because I think of it like if I am trying to map every single grain of sand on a beach,", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 26699, 341, 570, 286, 519, 295, 309, 411, 498, 286, 669, 1382, 281, 4471, 633, 2167, 12837, 295, 4932, 322, 257, 7534, 11, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.131342043195452, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144840235017167e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 18282, "start": 189.35999999999999, "end": 193.35999999999999, "text": " but the only tool I have is a standard 64 pack of crayons.", "tokens": [50692, 457, 264, 787, 2290, 286, 362, 307, 257, 3832, 12145, 2844, 295, 33073, 892, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.131342043195452, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144840235017167e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 18282, "start": 193.48, "end": 194.44, "text": " That's a great analogy.", "tokens": [50898, 663, 311, 257, 869, 21663, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.131342043195452, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144840235017167e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 18282, "start": 194.79999999999998, "end": 198.06, "text": " Right. So I am fundamentally forced to group things together.", "tokens": [50964, 1779, 13, 407, 286, 669, 17879, 7579, 281, 1594, 721, 1214, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.131342043195452, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144840235017167e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 19806, "start": 198.06, "end": 205.44, "text": " I might look down at a million slightly different shades of tan, beige, and white sand, but I only have one desert sand crayon.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 1062, 574, 760, 412, 257, 2459, 4748, 819, 20639, 295, 7603, 11, 40274, 11, 293, 2418, 4932, 11, 457, 286, 787, 362, 472, 11029, 4932, 33073, 266, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16209421157836915, "compression_ratio": 1.521505376344086, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556122370472767e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 19806, "start": 205.5, "end": 206.1, "text": " Yes, exactly.", "tokens": [50737, 1079, 11, 2293, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16209421157836915, "compression_ratio": 1.521505376344086, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556122370472767e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 19806, "start": 206.38, "end": 211.18, "text": " So all million of those unique individual grains get colored with the exact same crayon.", "tokens": [50781, 407, 439, 2459, 295, 729, 3845, 2609, 22908, 483, 14332, 365, 264, 1900, 912, 33073, 266, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16209421157836915, "compression_ratio": 1.521505376344086, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556122370472767e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 19806, "start": 211.64000000000001, "end": 214.08, "text": " I fundamentally lose the ability to tell them apart.", "tokens": [51044, 286, 17879, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 980, 552, 4936, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16209421157836915, "compression_ratio": 1.521505376344086, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556122370472767e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 21408, "start": 214.08, "end": 217.96, "text": " That is a brilliant way to visualize what Fliction calls a fiber.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 10248, 636, 281, 23273, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 257, 12874, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 21408, "start": 218.3, "end": 218.92000000000002, "text": " The fiber.", "tokens": [50576, 440, 12874, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 21408, "start": 219.14000000000001, "end": 227.24, "text": " Yes. A fiber is just a set of underlying realities or states that all collapse into a single observable category from the perspective of the system.", "tokens": [50618, 1079, 13, 316, 12874, 307, 445, 257, 992, 295, 14217, 27785, 420, 4368, 300, 439, 15584, 666, 257, 2167, 9951, 712, 7719, 490, 264, 4585, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 21408, "start": 227.42000000000002, "end": 227.56, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51032, 1033, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 21408, "start": 227.78, "end": 233.04000000000002, "text": " So all those millions of grains of sand are now one fiber, the desert sand fiber.", "tokens": [51050, 407, 439, 729, 6803, 295, 22908, 295, 4932, 366, 586, 472, 12874, 11, 264, 11029, 4932, 12874, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 21408, "start": 233.4, "end": 238.88000000000002, "text": " And this leads directly to a foundational proof in the text, which is the representation limit theorem.", "tokens": [51331, 400, 341, 6689, 3838, 281, 257, 32195, 8177, 294, 264, 2487, 11, 597, 307, 264, 10290, 4948, 20904, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 21408, "start": 239.04000000000002, "end": 242.9, "text": " Which basically says you can't cram infinity into a finite box, right?", "tokens": [51613, 3013, 1936, 1619, 291, 393, 380, 941, 335, 13202, 666, 257, 19362, 2424, 11, 558, 30, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649796086498815, "compression_ratio": 1.6430976430976432, "no_speech_prob": 1.244594271393451e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 24290, "start": 242.9, "end": 244.64000000000001, "text": " Precisely. It's the pigeonhole principle.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 467, 311, 264, 37886, 14094, 8665, 13, 50452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12730810688991173, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.325055841959466e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 24290, "start": 245.16, "end": 252.98000000000002, "text": " No finite representation, like your 64 crayons, can preserve every distinction of an infinite domain, like the physical beach.", "tokens": [50478, 883, 19362, 10290, 11, 411, 428, 12145, 33073, 892, 11, 393, 15665, 633, 16844, 295, 364, 13785, 9274, 11, 411, 264, 4001, 7534, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12730810688991173, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.325055841959466e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 24290, "start": 252.98000000000002, "end": 259.4, "text": " If you map an infinite number of real world states into a finite number of categories,", "tokens": [50869, 759, 291, 4471, 364, 13785, 1230, 295, 957, 1002, 4368, 666, 257, 19362, 1230, 295, 10479, 11, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12730810688991173, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.325055841959466e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 24290, "start": 259.7, "end": 266.22, "text": " you are mathematically guaranteed to assign infinitely many real states into at least one shared category.", "tokens": [51205, 291, 366, 44003, 18031, 281, 6269, 36227, 867, 957, 4368, 666, 412, 1935, 472, 5507, 7719, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12730810688991173, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.325055841959466e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 24290, "start": 266.62, "end": 270.66, "text": " Wow. So a blind spot isn't a design flaw. It's a mathematical necessity.", "tokens": [51551, 3153, 13, 407, 257, 6865, 4008, 1943, 380, 257, 1715, 13717, 13, 467, 311, 257, 18894, 24217, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12730810688991173, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.325055841959466e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 24290, "start": 270.92, "end": 271.22, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51766, 1079, 13, 51781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12730810688991173, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.325055841959466e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 27122, "start": 271.22, "end": 276.16, "text": " Like, if I'm building a self-driving car and its camera only has so many pixels,", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 478, 2390, 257, 2698, 12, 47094, 1032, 293, 1080, 2799, 787, 575, 370, 867, 18668, 11, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 27122, "start": 276.94000000000005, "end": 283.22, "text": " there is a physical limit where a floating plastic bag and a heavy rock become mathematically indistinguishable.", "tokens": [50651, 456, 307, 257, 4001, 4948, 689, 257, 12607, 5900, 3411, 293, 257, 4676, 3727, 1813, 44003, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 27122, "start": 283.86, "end": 287.68, "text": " Exactly. And the text actually gives us two different ways to measure that limitation.", "tokens": [50997, 7587, 13, 400, 264, 2487, 767, 2709, 505, 732, 819, 2098, 281, 3481, 300, 27432, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 27122, "start": 287.86, "end": 288.3, "text": " Let's take a word of it.", "tokens": [51197, 961, 311, 747, 257, 1349, 295, 309, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 27122, "start": 288.42, "end": 289.8, "text": " First is the coding deficit.", "tokens": [51225, 2386, 307, 264, 17720, 22132, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 27122, "start": 290.52000000000004, "end": 295.20000000000005, "text": " This measures how many bits of information you are wasting by using an inefficient description.", "tokens": [51330, 639, 8000, 577, 867, 9239, 295, 1589, 291, 366, 20457, 538, 1228, 364, 43495, 3855, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 27122, "start": 295.44000000000005, "end": 296.8, "text": " So sticking with the crayons.", "tokens": [51576, 407, 13465, 365, 264, 33073, 892, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1458467706903681, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552559019625268e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 29680, "start": 296.8, "end": 304.54, "text": " Right. Think of it as having your 64 crayons, but for some reason you are stubbornly only using three of them to draw the whole beach.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 1419, 428, 12145, 33073, 892, 11, 457, 337, 512, 1778, 291, 366, 24137, 356, 787, 1228, 1045, 295, 552, 281, 2642, 264, 1379, 7534, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11120142760100188, "compression_ratio": 1.5162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881443737540078e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 29680, "start": 304.68, "end": 308.82, "text": " I'm just leaving the other 61 crayons in the box, like wasting my own capacity.", "tokens": [50759, 286, 478, 445, 5012, 264, 661, 28294, 33073, 892, 294, 264, 2424, 11, 411, 20457, 452, 1065, 6042, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11120142760100188, "compression_ratio": 1.5162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881443737540078e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 29680, "start": 308.94, "end": 311.56, "text": " Exactly. But the second measure is the distinguishability deficit.", "tokens": [50972, 7587, 13, 583, 264, 1150, 3481, 307, 264, 20206, 2310, 22132, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11120142760100188, "compression_ratio": 1.5162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881443737540078e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 29680, "start": 312.14, "end": 314.04, "text": " This measures the inaccessible distinctions.", "tokens": [51132, 639, 8000, 264, 33230, 780, 964, 1483, 49798, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11120142760100188, "compression_ratio": 1.5162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881443737540078e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 31404, "start": 314.04, "end": 322.86, "text": " So even if you perfectly use all 64 crayons with maximum efficiency, there are still millions of shades of sand you literally cannot represent.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 754, 498, 291, 6239, 764, 439, 12145, 33073, 892, 365, 6674, 10493, 11, 456, 366, 920, 6803, 295, 20639, 295, 4932, 291, 3736, 2644, 2906, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626234351814568, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540872203550824e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 31404, "start": 322.98, "end": 324.18, "text": " Because you just don't have the colors.", "tokens": [50812, 1436, 291, 445, 500, 380, 362, 264, 4577, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626234351814568, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540872203550824e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 31404, "start": 324.34000000000003, "end": 324.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50880, 1779, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626234351814568, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540872203550824e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 31404, "start": 324.90000000000003, "end": 333.14000000000004, "text": " Wait, so if every system has these deficits inherently baked in, I mean, does that mean all systems are just fundamentally flawed from the start?", "tokens": [50908, 3802, 11, 370, 498, 633, 1185, 575, 613, 49616, 27993, 19453, 294, 11, 286, 914, 11, 775, 300, 914, 439, 3652, 366, 445, 17879, 38823, 490, 264, 722, 30, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626234351814568, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540872203550824e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 33314, "start": 333.14, "end": 334.06, "text": " It can feel that way.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 393, 841, 300, 636, 13, 50411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 33314, "start": 334.59999999999997, "end": 340.41999999999996, "text": " Are we all just walking around functionally blind, just hoping we don't trip over a rock that we categorized as a plastic bag?", "tokens": [50438, 2014, 321, 439, 445, 4494, 926, 2445, 379, 6865, 11, 445, 7159, 321, 500, 380, 4931, 670, 257, 3727, 300, 321, 19250, 1602, 382, 257, 5900, 3411, 30, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 33314, "start": 340.41999999999996, "end": 344.32, "text": " That is the natural human reaction to this idea, you know, to view it as a failure.", "tokens": [50729, 663, 307, 264, 3303, 1952, 5480, 281, 341, 1558, 11, 291, 458, 11, 281, 1910, 309, 382, 257, 7763, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 33314, "start": 344.5, "end": 346.53999999999996, "text": " But the text insists this is not a flaw.", "tokens": [50933, 583, 264, 2487, 50137, 341, 307, 406, 257, 13717, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 33314, "start": 346.82, "end": 350.15999999999997, "text": " It is the absolute basis of information theory.", "tokens": [51049, 467, 307, 264, 8236, 5143, 295, 1589, 5261, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 33314, "start": 350.38, "end": 350.53999999999996, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51227, 1033, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 33314, "start": 351.44, "end": 353.34, "text": " Fliction cites the compression theorem.", "tokens": [51280, 3235, 4105, 269, 3324, 264, 19355, 20904, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 33314, "start": 353.82, "end": 356.3, "text": " It states that every representation compresses.", "tokens": [51399, 467, 4368, 300, 633, 10290, 14778, 279, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 33314, "start": 356.84, "end": 359.47999999999996, "text": " Every mental model you have compresses reality.", "tokens": [51550, 2048, 4973, 2316, 291, 362, 14778, 279, 4103, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 33314, "start": 359.62, "end": 360.32, "text": " Because it has to.", "tokens": [51689, 1436, 309, 575, 281, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 33314, "start": 360.46, "end": 360.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51731, 1079, 13, 51743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 33314, "start": 360.82, "end": 360.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51749, 1779, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1722130810772931, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 36096, "start": 360.96, "end": 363.14, "text": " Every scientific theory compresses data.", "tokens": [50365, 2048, 8134, 5261, 14778, 279, 1412, 13, 50474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 36096, "start": 363.59999999999997, "end": 371.58, "text": " Compression is the only way a finite mind or a finite system can operate in an infinite universe without being instantly paralyzed by noise.", "tokens": [50497, 6620, 2775, 307, 264, 787, 636, 257, 19362, 1575, 420, 257, 19362, 1185, 393, 9651, 294, 364, 13785, 6445, 1553, 885, 13518, 41919, 538, 5658, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 36096, "start": 371.65999999999997, "end": 372.09999999999997, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [50900, 876, 11, 558, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 36096, "start": 372.21999999999997, "end": 376.35999999999996, "text": " Because if I try to process every grain of sand individually, my brain would just crash.", "tokens": [50928, 1436, 498, 286, 853, 281, 1399, 633, 12837, 295, 4932, 16652, 11, 452, 3567, 576, 445, 8252, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 36096, "start": 376.85999999999996, "end": 377.34, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51160, 7587, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 36096, "start": 377.58, "end": 379.62, "text": " The question isn't whether compression occurs.", "tokens": [51196, 440, 1168, 1943, 380, 1968, 19355, 11843, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 36096, "start": 379.62, "end": 383.2, "text": " The question is which distinctions survive the compression.", "tokens": [51298, 440, 1168, 307, 597, 1483, 49798, 7867, 264, 19355, 13, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 36096, "start": 383.64, "end": 385.94, "text": " And those survive distinctions aren't static.", "tokens": [51499, 400, 729, 7867, 1483, 49798, 3212, 380, 13437, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 36096, "start": 386.12, "end": 386.34, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51623, 1779, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 36096, "start": 386.4, "end": 386.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51637, 1779, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17999539808793502, "compression_ratio": 1.6925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920832360794002e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 38658, "start": 386.58, "end": 389.52, "text": " Because, I mean, I can learn.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 11, 286, 914, 11, 286, 393, 1466, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 38658, "start": 390.15999999999997, "end": 391.26, "text": " My categories can change.", "tokens": [50544, 1222, 10479, 393, 1319, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 38658, "start": 391.3, "end": 395.26, "text": " If I'm a system, how do I actually change what I can tell apart?", "tokens": [50601, 759, 286, 478, 257, 1185, 11, 577, 360, 286, 767, 1319, 437, 286, 393, 980, 4936, 30, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 38658, "start": 395.62, "end": 402.03999999999996, "text": " The text outlines four, and only four, mathematical operations that can change a distinguishability structure.", "tokens": [50817, 440, 2487, 40125, 1451, 11, 293, 787, 1451, 11, 18894, 7705, 300, 393, 1319, 257, 20206, 2310, 3877, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 38658, "start": 402.79999999999995, "end": 404.71999999999997, "text": " Let's stick with your map of the beach.", "tokens": [51176, 961, 311, 2897, 365, 428, 4471, 295, 264, 7534, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 38658, "start": 404.91999999999996, "end": 405.15999999999997, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51282, 1033, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 38658, "start": 405.2, "end": 405.88, "text": " I like the beach.", "tokens": [51296, 286, 411, 264, 7534, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 38658, "start": 406.06, "end": 407.65999999999997, "text": " Operation one is projection.", "tokens": [51339, 27946, 472, 307, 22743, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 38658, "start": 408.14, "end": 409.52, "text": " This merges fibers together.", "tokens": [51443, 639, 3551, 2880, 25252, 1214, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17339807627152423, "compression_ratio": 1.5414847161572052, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406820141906306e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 40952, "start": 409.52, "end": 416.0, "text": " Let's say you decide you just don't care about the difference between the desert sand crayon and the macaroni and cheese crayon.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 291, 4536, 291, 445, 500, 380, 1127, 466, 264, 2649, 1296, 264, 11029, 4932, 33073, 266, 293, 264, 49686, 72, 293, 5399, 33073, 266, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 40952, "start": 416.15999999999997, "end": 417.26, "text": " I just call them both yellow.", "tokens": [50697, 286, 445, 818, 552, 1293, 5566, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 40952, "start": 417.65999999999997, "end": 418.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50772, 1079, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 40952, "start": 418.2, "end": 419.97999999999996, "text": " You have actively lost a distinction.", "tokens": [50799, 509, 362, 13022, 2731, 257, 16844, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 40952, "start": 420.56, "end": 421.88, "text": " Your map just got coarser.", "tokens": [50917, 2260, 4471, 445, 658, 598, 685, 260, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 40952, "start": 422.0, "end": 422.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50989, 1779, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 40952, "start": 422.62, "end": 427.06, "text": " But sometimes you need a coarser map if you're just trying to find the ocean, not a specific seashell.", "tokens": [51020, 583, 2171, 291, 643, 257, 598, 685, 260, 4471, 498, 291, 434, 445, 1382, 281, 915, 264, 7810, 11, 406, 257, 2685, 22535, 21288, 13, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 40952, "start": 427.38, "end": 427.85999999999996, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51258, 7587, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 40952, "start": 428.34, "end": 431.09999999999997, "text": " Sometimes less detail is better for a specific task.", "tokens": [51306, 4803, 1570, 2607, 307, 1101, 337, 257, 2685, 5633, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 40952, "start": 431.15999999999997, "end": 432.32, "text": " So what's the second operation?", "tokens": [51447, 407, 437, 311, 264, 1150, 6916, 30, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 40952, "start": 433.0, "end": 433.44, "text": " Embedding.", "tokens": [51539, 24234, 292, 3584, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 40952, "start": 433.52, "end": 434.62, "text": " This is separating fibers.", "tokens": [51565, 639, 307, 29279, 25252, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17680449234811882, "compression_ratio": 1.6262975778546713, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776675976574394e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 43462, "start": 434.62, "end": 438.22, "text": " This is you going to the store and buying the 128 pack of crayons.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 291, 516, 281, 264, 3531, 293, 6382, 264, 29810, 2844, 295, 33073, 892, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 43462, "start": 438.34000000000003, "end": 438.86, "text": " Oh, nice.", "tokens": [50551, 876, 11, 1481, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 43462, "start": 439.18, "end": 439.86, "text": " An upgrade.", "tokens": [50593, 1107, 11484, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 43462, "start": 440.34000000000003, "end": 443.62, "text": " You can suddenly draw a line between almond and desert sand.", "tokens": [50651, 509, 393, 5800, 2642, 257, 1622, 1296, 29506, 293, 11029, 4932, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 43462, "start": 444.22, "end": 447.92, "text": " You are making finer distinctions that were previously impossible for you.", "tokens": [50845, 509, 366, 1455, 39130, 1483, 49798, 300, 645, 8046, 6243, 337, 291, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 43462, "start": 448.32, "end": 448.56, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51050, 1033, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 43462, "start": 448.72, "end": 450.46, "text": " So projection makes it blurry.", "tokens": [51070, 407, 22743, 1669, 309, 37644, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 43462, "start": 450.96, "end": 452.0, "text": " Embedding makes it sharper.", "tokens": [51182, 24234, 292, 3584, 1669, 309, 44670, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 43462, "start": 452.78000000000003, "end": 453.14, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51273, 5803, 309, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 43462, "start": 453.24, "end": 455.36, "text": " Operation three takes it to another level.", "tokens": [51296, 27946, 1045, 2516, 309, 281, 1071, 1496, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 43462, "start": 455.52, "end": 455.92, "text": " Revision.", "tokens": [51410, 1300, 6763, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 43462, "start": 456.2, "end": 456.58, "text": " Revision.", "tokens": [51444, 1300, 6763, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 43462, "start": 456.84000000000003, "end": 457.12, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51476, 1033, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 43462, "start": 457.32, "end": 459.6, "text": " This is changing the generating ontology entirely.", "tokens": [51500, 639, 307, 4473, 264, 17746, 6592, 1793, 7696, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21001569889793711, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457144469944393e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 45960, "start": 459.6, "end": 466.40000000000003, "text": " So instead of using crayons to map color, you bring a chemical spectrometer to the beach to map mineral composition.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 2602, 295, 1228, 33073, 892, 281, 4471, 2017, 11, 291, 1565, 257, 7313, 6177, 81, 13606, 281, 264, 7534, 281, 4471, 21630, 12686, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 45960, "start": 466.90000000000003, "end": 467.16, "text": " Whoa.", "tokens": [50730, 7521, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 45960, "start": 467.48, "end": 470.74, "text": " So I'm not just making finer or coarser color choices anymore.", "tokens": [50759, 407, 286, 478, 406, 445, 1455, 39130, 420, 598, 685, 260, 2017, 7994, 3602, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 45960, "start": 470.84000000000003, "end": 471.02000000000004, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50927, 883, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 45960, "start": 471.12, "end": 474.84000000000003, "text": " You are changing the entire language of how you describe reality.", "tokens": [50941, 509, 366, 4473, 264, 2302, 2856, 295, 577, 291, 6786, 4103, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 45960, "start": 475.04, "end": 477.62, "text": " You change the rules of what a distinction even means.", "tokens": [51137, 509, 1319, 264, 4474, 295, 437, 257, 16844, 754, 1355, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 45960, "start": 477.96000000000004, "end": 478.64000000000004, "text": " That's really cool.", "tokens": [51283, 663, 311, 534, 1627, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 45960, "start": 478.72, "end": 478.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51321, 1079, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 45960, "start": 479.54, "end": 481.04, "text": " And the final operation is transport.", "tokens": [51362, 400, 264, 2572, 6916, 307, 5495, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 45960, "start": 481.32000000000005, "end": 484.28000000000003, "text": " This is connecting two entirely distinct spaces.", "tokens": [51451, 639, 307, 11015, 732, 7696, 10644, 7673, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 45960, "start": 484.8, "end": 486.94, "text": " It is essentially reasoning by analogy.", "tokens": [51625, 467, 307, 4476, 21577, 538, 21663, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509151776631673, "compression_ratio": 1.6382978723404256, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191761694108297e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 48694, "start": 486.94, "end": 489.66, "text": " Like taking what I learned on the beach and applying it somewhere else.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 1940, 437, 286, 3264, 322, 264, 7534, 293, 9275, 309, 4079, 1646, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 48694, "start": 489.86, "end": 490.3, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50511, 48746, 736, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 48694, "start": 490.54, "end": 494.58, "text": " You take the distinguishability structure you built for the sand on the beach and you map", "tokens": [50545, 509, 747, 264, 20206, 2310, 3877, 291, 3094, 337, 264, 4932, 322, 264, 7534, 293, 291, 4471, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 48694, "start": 494.58, "end": 499.46, "text": " it onto a snow drift in the mountains to see if the aerodynamic patterns of the wind hold up.", "tokens": [50747, 309, 3911, 257, 5756, 19699, 294, 264, 10233, 281, 536, 498, 264, 11207, 34988, 8294, 295, 264, 2468, 1797, 493, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 48694, "start": 499.72, "end": 505.78, "text": " And the text mathematically proves that projection, embedding, revision, and transport are the exhaustive", "tokens": [51004, 400, 264, 2487, 44003, 25019, 300, 22743, 11, 12240, 3584, 11, 34218, 11, 293, 5495, 366, 264, 14687, 488, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 48694, "start": 505.78, "end": 508.72, "text": " possibilities for how any system's perception can change.", "tokens": [51307, 12178, 337, 577, 604, 1185, 311, 12860, 393, 1319, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 48694, "start": 509.12, "end": 513.44, "text": " So if a system is fundamentally just a collection of these blind spots and these changing instinctions,", "tokens": [51474, 407, 498, 257, 1185, 307, 17879, 445, 257, 5765, 295, 613, 6865, 10681, 293, 613, 4473, 1058, 49798, 11, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09348947861615349, "compression_ratio": 1.6898734177215189, "no_speech_prob": 1.927891223399425e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 51344, "start": 513.44, "end": 517.34, "text": " it basically has to use whatever it can see to establish its rules.", "tokens": [50365, 309, 1936, 575, 281, 764, 2035, 309, 393, 536, 281, 8327, 1080, 4474, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 51344, "start": 517.58, "end": 518.46, "text": " It has no other choice.", "tokens": [50572, 467, 575, 572, 661, 3922, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 51344, "start": 518.72, "end": 518.9000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50629, 1779, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 51344, "start": 519.08, "end": 524.3800000000001, "text": " Like if I can only see 64 colors, I have to base my entire survival strategy on those 64 colors.", "tokens": [50647, 1743, 498, 286, 393, 787, 536, 12145, 4577, 11, 286, 362, 281, 3096, 452, 2302, 12559, 5206, 322, 729, 12145, 4577, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 51344, "start": 524.5200000000001, "end": 530.22, "text": " Which takes us into how systems actually set boundaries, which Fliction calls admissibility.", "tokens": [50919, 3013, 2516, 505, 666, 577, 3652, 767, 992, 13180, 11, 597, 3235, 4105, 5498, 5910, 891, 2841, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 51344, "start": 530.6400000000001, "end": 530.9000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51225, 1079, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 51344, "start": 531.08, "end": 533.2800000000001, "text": " Admissibility is a huge concept here.", "tokens": [51247, 46292, 891, 2841, 307, 257, 2603, 3410, 510, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 51344, "start": 533.6600000000001, "end": 538.86, "text": " It is the set of rules that specifies which transitions between states are reachable or permitted.", "tokens": [51376, 467, 307, 264, 992, 295, 4474, 300, 1608, 11221, 597, 23767, 1296, 4368, 366, 2524, 712, 420, 28658, 13, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 51344, "start": 538.9000000000001, "end": 539.22, "text": " Permitted.", "tokens": [51638, 41006, 3944, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521248195482337, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 2.004714319894796e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 53922, "start": 539.22, "end": 545.02, "text": " If a system is at state A, admissibility dictates whether it is physically, legally, or logically", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 1185, 307, 412, 1785, 316, 11, 5910, 891, 2841, 12569, 1024, 1968, 309, 307, 9762, 11, 21106, 11, 420, 38887, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 53922, "start": 545.02, "end": 549.1600000000001, "text": " allowed to move to state B. It is the viability boundary of the system.", "tokens": [50655, 4350, 281, 1286, 281, 1785, 363, 13, 467, 307, 264, 1932, 2310, 12866, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 53922, "start": 549.28, "end": 550.1800000000001, "text": " It's the guardrails.", "tokens": [50868, 467, 311, 264, 6290, 424, 4174, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 53922, "start": 550.48, "end": 550.96, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50928, 7587, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 53922, "start": 551.08, "end": 555.52, "text": " But reading through the text, Fliction points out there are actually two totally different", "tokens": [50958, 583, 3760, 807, 264, 2487, 11, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 456, 366, 767, 732, 3879, 819, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 53922, "start": 555.52, "end": 561.1600000000001, "text": " ways to define what makes a state admissible. And they leave it as this massive open question", "tokens": [51180, 2098, 281, 6964, 437, 1669, 257, 1785, 5910, 41073, 13, 400, 436, 1856, 309, 382, 341, 5994, 1269, 1168, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 53922, "start": 561.1600000000001, "end": 566.74, "text": " whether these two ways even agree with each other. It is arguably the central open problem", "tokens": [51462, 1968, 613, 732, 2098, 754, 3986, 365, 1184, 661, 13, 467, 307, 26771, 264, 5777, 1269, 1154, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08743703776392443, "compression_ratio": 1.690391459074733, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490564339402547e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 56674, "start": 566.74, "end": 567.86, "text": " of the entire volume.", "tokens": [50365, 295, 264, 2302, 5523, 13, 50421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 56674, "start": 568.5, "end": 569.3, "text": " Break it down for us.", "tokens": [50453, 16925, 309, 760, 337, 505, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 56674, "start": 569.7, "end": 574.8, "text": " The first definition is deficit-based. A state is inadmissible if your system literally cannot", "tokens": [50513, 440, 700, 7123, 307, 22132, 12, 6032, 13, 316, 1785, 307, 42148, 76, 41073, 498, 428, 1185, 3736, 2644, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 56674, "start": 574.8, "end": 576.26, "text": " represent it without an error.", "tokens": [50768, 2906, 309, 1553, 364, 6713, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 56674, "start": 576.72, "end": 583.1, "text": " So back to the crayons. If your rules require a neon green crayon to proceed and you only have", "tokens": [50864, 407, 646, 281, 264, 33073, 892, 13, 759, 428, 4474, 3651, 257, 30820, 3092, 33073, 266, 281, 8991, 293, 291, 787, 362, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 56674, "start": 583.1, "end": 584.16, "text": " the 64-pack.", "tokens": [51183, 264, 12145, 12, 9539, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 56674, "start": 584.74, "end": 588.12, "text": " That future state is deficit inadmissible.", "tokens": [51265, 663, 2027, 1785, 307, 22132, 42148, 76, 41073, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20094017548994583, "compression_ratio": 1.5533980582524272, "no_speech_prob": 1.466476462833044e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 58812, "start": 588.12, "end": 591.54, "text": " You literally can't comprehend the rule so you can't follow it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 3736, 393, 380, 38183, 264, 4978, 370, 291, 393, 380, 1524, 309, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 58812, "start": 591.54, "end": 596.48, "text": " Right. You don't have the language for it. The second definition, however, is entropy", "tokens": [50536, 1779, 13, 509, 500, 380, 362, 264, 2856, 337, 309, 13, 440, 1150, 7123, 11, 4461, 11, 307, 30867, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 58812, "start": 596.48, "end": 597.84, "text": " monotonicity-based.", "tokens": [50783, 1108, 310, 11630, 507, 12, 6032, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 58812, "start": 598.0600000000001, "end": 599.3, "text": " That sounds intense.", "tokens": [50862, 663, 3263, 9447, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 58812, "start": 599.36, "end": 603.92, "text": " It sounds complex, but it just means a state is admissible if there is a thermodynamic or", "tokens": [50927, 467, 3263, 3997, 11, 457, 309, 445, 1355, 257, 1785, 307, 5910, 41073, 498, 456, 307, 257, 8810, 34988, 420, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 58812, "start": 603.92, "end": 608.7, "text": " informational path to it where entropy does not decrease. This is rooted more in traditional", "tokens": [51155, 49391, 3100, 281, 309, 689, 30867, 775, 406, 11514, 13, 639, 307, 25277, 544, 294, 5164, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 58812, "start": 608.7, "end": 609.2, "text": " physics.", "tokens": [51394, 10649, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 58812, "start": 609.36, "end": 614.84, "text": " Okay. So the arrow of time, basically. And the author doesn't resolve if these two, the crayon", "tokens": [51427, 1033, 13, 407, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 11, 1936, 13, 400, 264, 3793, 1177, 380, 14151, 498, 613, 732, 11, 264, 33073, 266, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377480979857406, "compression_ratio": 1.627986348122867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856431835950535e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 61484, "start": 614.84, "end": 616.76, "text": " one and the physics one are the exact same thing.", "tokens": [50365, 472, 293, 264, 10649, 472, 366, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 61484, "start": 616.82, "end": 622.96, "text": " They refuse to. And they provide a deeply insightful reason for their skepticism based on Hamiltonian", "tokens": [50464, 814, 16791, 281, 13, 400, 436, 2893, 257, 8760, 46401, 1778, 337, 641, 19128, 26356, 2361, 322, 18484, 952, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 61484, "start": 622.96, "end": 623.46, "text": " mechanics.", "tokens": [50771, 12939, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 61484, "start": 623.62, "end": 624.4, "text": " Okay. Physics time.", "tokens": [50804, 1033, 13, 38355, 565, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 61484, "start": 624.74, "end": 629.82, "text": " In classical physics, you have constants of motion. Think of the total energy of a swinging", "tokens": [50860, 682, 13735, 10649, 11, 291, 362, 35870, 295, 5394, 13, 6557, 295, 264, 3217, 2281, 295, 257, 29500, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 61484, "start": 629.82, "end": 634.86, "text": " pendulum. The total energy stays exactly the same as the pendulum swings back and forth.", "tokens": [51114, 44103, 13, 440, 3217, 2281, 10834, 2293, 264, 912, 382, 264, 44103, 32386, 646, 293, 5220, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 61484, "start": 634.88, "end": 638.64, "text": " Right. Conservation of energy. It never loses energy in a perfect system.", "tokens": [51367, 1779, 13, 40131, 295, 2281, 13, 467, 1128, 18293, 2281, 294, 257, 2176, 1185, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 61484, "start": 638.64, "end": 643.64, "text": " But knowing the total energy is 10 joules doesn't tell you where the pendulum is right now.", "tokens": [51555, 583, 5276, 264, 3217, 2281, 307, 1266, 11110, 904, 1177, 380, 980, 291, 689, 264, 44103, 307, 558, 586, 13, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047123718261718, "compression_ratio": 1.723127035830619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977228220998008e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 64364, "start": 643.64, "end": 645.84, "text": " Is it at the top of the swing? Is it at the bottom?", "tokens": [50365, 1119, 309, 412, 264, 1192, 295, 264, 11173, 30, 1119, 309, 412, 264, 2767, 30, 50475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 64364, "start": 646.04, "end": 646.54, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50485, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 64364, "start": 646.88, "end": 652.6999999999999, "text": " Constants of motion are inherently non-injective. They group many different physical positions", "tokens": [50527, 8574, 1719, 295, 5394, 366, 27993, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 13, 814, 1594, 867, 819, 4001, 8432, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 64364, "start": 652.6999999999999, "end": 656.38, "text": " into one single number. They don't separate things. They merge them.", "tokens": [50818, 666, 472, 2167, 1230, 13, 814, 500, 380, 4994, 721, 13, 814, 22183, 552, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 64364, "start": 656.48, "end": 662.98, "text": " But a history channel, which the deficit-based admissibility relies on, is valuable precisely", "tokens": [51007, 583, 257, 2503, 2269, 11, 597, 264, 22132, 12, 6032, 5910, 891, 2841, 30910, 322, 11, 307, 8263, 13402, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 64364, "start": 662.98, "end": 664.8199999999999, "text": " because it separates trajectories.", "tokens": [51332, 570, 309, 34149, 18257, 2083, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 64364, "start": 664.96, "end": 667.38, "text": " Yes. It needs to tell you exactly how you got here.", "tokens": [51431, 1079, 13, 467, 2203, 281, 980, 291, 2293, 577, 291, 658, 510, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 64364, "start": 667.52, "end": 672.46, "text": " Ah. So the physics definition is built to group things together. But the information definition", "tokens": [51559, 2438, 13, 407, 264, 10649, 7123, 307, 3094, 281, 1594, 721, 1214, 13, 583, 264, 1589, 7123, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08379727318173363, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499295841191033e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 67246, "start": 672.46, "end": 676.48, "text": " is built to tell things apart. They are fundamentally doing opposite jobs.", "tokens": [50365, 307, 3094, 281, 980, 721, 4936, 13, 814, 366, 17879, 884, 6182, 4782, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14065257790162392, "compression_ratio": 1.5593869731800767, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275544059516812e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 67246, "start": 676.48, "end": 682.3000000000001, "text": " It is a profound demonstration of Fliction's mathematical discipline. They refuse to assume", "tokens": [50566, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 16520, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 18894, 13635, 13, 814, 16791, 281, 6552, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14065257790162392, "compression_ratio": 1.5593869731800767, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275544059516812e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 67246, "start": 682.3000000000001, "end": 685.7800000000001, "text": " two frameworks are identical just because they both define a boundary.", "tokens": [50857, 732, 29834, 366, 14800, 445, 570, 436, 1293, 6964, 257, 12866, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14065257790162392, "compression_ratio": 1.5593869731800767, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275544059516812e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 67246, "start": 686.38, "end": 692.0, "text": " I respect that discipline. That's really rigorous. But, you know, a system rarely has just one rule,", "tokens": [51061, 286, 3104, 300, 13635, 13, 663, 311, 534, 29882, 13, 583, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 1185, 13752, 575, 445, 472, 4978, 11, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14065257790162392, "compression_ratio": 1.5593869731800767, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275544059516812e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 67246, "start": 692.24, "end": 695.44, "text": " right? A city doesn't survive because of one law.", "tokens": [51354, 558, 30, 316, 2307, 1177, 380, 7867, 570, 295, 472, 2101, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14065257790162392, "compression_ratio": 1.5593869731800767, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275544059516812e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 67246, "start": 695.58, "end": 696.5400000000001, "text": " No, of course not.", "tokens": [51521, 883, 11, 295, 1164, 406, 13, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14065257790162392, "compression_ratio": 1.5593869731800767, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275544059516812e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 69654, "start": 696.54, "end": 702.62, "text": " It has building codes, zoning laws, fire inspections, health codes. The text moves from", "tokens": [50365, 467, 575, 2390, 14211, 11, 37184, 6064, 11, 2610, 46544, 11, 1585, 14211, 13, 440, 2487, 6067, 490, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10639163885223732, "compression_ratio": 1.6008583690987124, "no_speech_prob": 1.668484903190326e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 69654, "start": 702.62, "end": 709.5, "text": " a single constraint to what it calls constraint populations. And it describes them as sympoetic", "tokens": [50669, 257, 2167, 25534, 281, 437, 309, 5498, 25534, 12822, 13, 400, 309, 15626, 552, 382, 6697, 2259, 3532, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10639163885223732, "compression_ratio": 1.6008583690987124, "no_speech_prob": 1.668484903190326e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 69654, "start": 709.5, "end": 710.0999999999999, "text": " systems.", "tokens": [51013, 3652, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10639163885223732, "compression_ratio": 1.6008583690987124, "no_speech_prob": 1.668484903190326e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 69654, "start": 710.36, "end": 716.0, "text": " Sympoetic. It means making with or collectively producing. In a sympoetic system, the rules", "tokens": [51056, 28877, 2259, 3532, 13, 467, 1355, 1455, 365, 420, 24341, 10501, 13, 682, 257, 6697, 2259, 3532, 1185, 11, 264, 4474, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10639163885223732, "compression_ratio": 1.6008583690987124, "no_speech_prob": 1.668484903190326e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 69654, "start": 716.0, "end": 721.2199999999999, "text": " don't just act independently. They update based on the joint state of the system itself.", "tokens": [51338, 500, 380, 445, 605, 21761, 13, 814, 5623, 2361, 322, 264, 7225, 1785, 295, 264, 1185, 2564, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10639163885223732, "compression_ratio": 1.6008583690987124, "no_speech_prob": 1.668484903190326e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 72122, "start": 721.22, "end": 722.14, "text": " So they're reactive.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 434, 28897, 13, 50411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 72122, "start": 722.24, "end": 724.72, "text": " Highly reactive. This is level three behavior.", "tokens": [50416, 5229, 356, 28897, 13, 639, 307, 1496, 1045, 5223, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 72122, "start": 724.94, "end": 726.52, "text": " Give me a real world example of that.", "tokens": [50551, 5303, 385, 257, 957, 1002, 1365, 295, 300, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 72122, "start": 726.74, "end": 727.62, "text": " Think of a tax cut.", "tokens": [50641, 6557, 295, 257, 3366, 1723, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 72122, "start": 727.9, "end": 728.5, "text": " Oh, perfect.", "tokens": [50699, 876, 11, 2176, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 72122, "start": 728.82, "end": 731.82, "text": " The government sets a rule. Accountants find a loophole.", "tokens": [50745, 440, 2463, 6352, 257, 4978, 13, 24558, 1719, 915, 257, 6367, 14094, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 72122, "start": 731.98, "end": 732.98, "text": " As they always do.", "tokens": [50903, 1018, 436, 1009, 360, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 72122, "start": 733.1600000000001, "end": 738.2, "text": " Right. And then the joint state of the system, the economy, changes based on that loophole.", "tokens": [50962, 1779, 13, 400, 550, 264, 7225, 1785, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 264, 5010, 11, 2962, 2361, 322, 300, 6367, 14094, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 72122, "start": 738.74, "end": 743.12, "text": " The government then authors a new rule to close the loophole, which changes the behavior", "tokens": [51241, 440, 2463, 550, 16552, 257, 777, 4978, 281, 1998, 264, 6367, 14094, 11, 597, 2962, 264, 5223, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 72122, "start": 743.12, "end": 743.5400000000001, "text": " again.", "tokens": [51460, 797, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 72122, "start": 743.6800000000001, "end": 747.96, "text": " So the population of constraints is constantly rewriting itself based on the game being played?", "tokens": [51488, 407, 264, 4415, 295, 18491, 307, 6460, 319, 19868, 2564, 2361, 322, 264, 1216, 885, 3737, 30, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 72122, "start": 747.96, "end": 750.64, "text": " Yes. It's a dynamic ecology of rules.", "tokens": [51702, 1079, 13, 467, 311, 257, 8546, 39683, 295, 4474, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518036151754445, "compression_ratio": 1.7234726688102895, "no_speech_prob": 1.846848195208306e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 75064, "start": 750.64, "end": 756.06, "text": " Which sounds incredibly robust. I mean, that sounds great. But here is where the text introduces", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 3263, 6252, 13956, 13, 286, 914, 11, 300, 3263, 869, 13, 583, 510, 307, 689, 264, 2487, 31472, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463169097900391, "compression_ratio": 1.6192170818505338, "no_speech_prob": 1.4385164066876843e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 75064, "start": 756.06, "end": 761.9, "text": " something I found utterly terrifying. It's this mathematical trap called the masking pathology.", "tokens": [50636, 746, 286, 1352, 30251, 18106, 13, 467, 311, 341, 18894, 11487, 1219, 264, 31226, 3100, 1793, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463169097900391, "compression_ratio": 1.6192170818505338, "no_speech_prob": 1.4385164066876843e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 75064, "start": 762.52, "end": 767.0, "text": " Yes. The diversity score. Denoted mathematically as D-Chi.", "tokens": [50959, 1079, 13, 440, 8811, 6175, 13, 6458, 23325, 44003, 382, 413, 12, 34, 4954, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463169097900391, "compression_ratio": 1.6192170818505338, "no_speech_prob": 1.4385164066876843e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 75064, "start": 767.14, "end": 767.3199999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51190, 1779, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463169097900391, "compression_ratio": 1.6192170818505338, "no_speech_prob": 1.4385164066876843e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 75064, "start": 767.5, "end": 772.74, "text": " When you have a population of rules, you naturally want diversity, correct? You want different rules", "tokens": [51208, 1133, 291, 362, 257, 4415, 295, 4474, 11, 291, 8195, 528, 8811, 11, 3006, 30, 509, 528, 819, 4474, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463169097900391, "compression_ratio": 1.6192170818505338, "no_speech_prob": 1.4385164066876843e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 75064, "start": 772.74, "end": 777.52, "text": " catching different kinds of errors. So a single point of failure doesn't bring down the system.", "tokens": [51470, 16124, 819, 3685, 295, 13603, 13, 407, 257, 2167, 935, 295, 7763, 1177, 380, 1565, 760, 264, 1185, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463169097900391, "compression_ratio": 1.6192170818505338, "no_speech_prob": 1.4385164066876843e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 77752, "start": 777.52, "end": 782.52, "text": " Absolutely. Like a bank's fraud detection system. You don't want five algorithms checking if the", "tokens": [50365, 7021, 13, 1743, 257, 3765, 311, 14560, 17784, 1185, 13, 509, 500, 380, 528, 1732, 14642, 8568, 498, 264, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09341915794040846, "compression_ratio": 1.0666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.2063020938049562e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 78252, "start": 782.52, "end": 787.3, "text": " password is correct. And zero algorithms checking if the login is coming from a known IP address.", "tokens": [50365, 11524, 307, 3006, 13, 400, 4018, 14642, 8568, 498, 264, 24276, 307, 1348, 490, 257, 2570, 8671, 2985, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19942601025104523, "compression_ratio": 1.507936507936508, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012526811963856e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 78252, "start": 787.66, "end": 788.54, "text": " You want diverse checks.", "tokens": [50622, 509, 528, 9521, 13834, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19942601025104523, "compression_ratio": 1.507936507936508, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012526811963856e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 78252, "start": 789.1, "end": 793.42, "text": " So systems use a mathematical formula to calculate the diversity of their constraints.", "tokens": [50694, 407, 3652, 764, 257, 18894, 8513, 281, 8873, 264, 8811, 295, 641, 18491, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19942601025104523, "compression_ratio": 1.507936507936508, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012526811963856e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 78252, "start": 793.66, "end": 797.6, "text": " It measures the average pairwise correlation of their failure events.", "tokens": [50922, 467, 8000, 264, 4274, 6119, 3711, 20009, 295, 641, 7763, 3931, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19942601025104523, "compression_ratio": 1.507936507936508, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012526811963856e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 78252, "start": 797.74, "end": 798.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51126, 1033, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19942601025104523, "compression_ratio": 1.507936507936508, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012526811963856e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 79802, "start": 798.02, "end": 803.04, "text": " Infliction provides a devastating proof of how this formula can completely, totally lie to you.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 3423, 4105, 6417, 257, 21280, 8177, 295, 577, 341, 8513, 393, 2584, 11, 3879, 4544, 281, 291, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 79802, "start": 803.36, "end": 805.52, "text": " Let's walk through the hypothetical scenario they present.", "tokens": [50632, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 264, 33053, 9005, 436, 1974, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 79802, "start": 805.62, "end": 807.22, "text": " Yeah, let's do it because this blew my mind.", "tokens": [50745, 865, 11, 718, 311, 360, 309, 570, 341, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 79802, "start": 807.3, "end": 811.9, "text": " Imagine a state space of eight possible actions a user can take, numbered one through eight.", "tokens": [50829, 11739, 257, 1785, 1901, 295, 3180, 1944, 5909, 257, 4195, 393, 747, 11, 40936, 472, 807, 3180, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 79802, "start": 812.04, "end": 812.9, "text": " Okay, one through eight.", "tokens": [51066, 1033, 11, 472, 807, 3180, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 79802, "start": 813.16, "end": 816.9399999999999, "text": " And the system has four security constraints evaluating these actions.", "tokens": [51122, 400, 264, 1185, 575, 1451, 3825, 18491, 27479, 613, 5909, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 79802, "start": 817.5799999999999, "end": 821.4399999999999, "text": " Constraints one, two, and three all admit actions one, two, three, and four.", "tokens": [51343, 8574, 424, 8654, 472, 11, 732, 11, 293, 1045, 439, 9796, 5909, 472, 11, 732, 11, 1045, 11, 293, 1451, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.139661054695602, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.564241137134604e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 82144, "start": 821.44, "end": 825.1600000000001, "text": " And they all perfectly reject actions five, six, seven, and eight.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 436, 439, 6239, 8248, 5909, 1732, 11, 2309, 11, 3407, 11, 293, 3180, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12984624151456153, "compression_ratio": 1.875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617380214911659e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 82144, "start": 825.3000000000001, "end": 829.7800000000001, "text": " So they are identical. Constraints one, two, and three are just completely redundant copies of each other.", "tokens": [50558, 407, 436, 366, 14800, 13, 8574, 424, 8654, 472, 11, 732, 11, 293, 1045, 366, 445, 2584, 40997, 14341, 295, 1184, 661, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12984624151456153, "compression_ratio": 1.875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617380214911659e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 82144, "start": 829.9000000000001, "end": 835.0200000000001, "text": " Yes. But constraint four is the exact opposite. It admits five, six, seven, and eight.", "tokens": [50788, 1079, 13, 583, 25534, 1451, 307, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 467, 46682, 1732, 11, 2309, 11, 3407, 11, 293, 3180, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12984624151456153, "compression_ratio": 1.875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617380214911659e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 82144, "start": 835.2, "end": 838.1400000000001, "text": " And it vehemently rejects one, two, three, and four.", "tokens": [51053, 400, 309, 4221, 1712, 356, 8248, 82, 472, 11, 732, 11, 1045, 11, 293, 1451, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12984624151456153, "compression_ratio": 1.875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617380214911659e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 82144, "start": 838.24, "end": 842.46, "text": " Wait, wait, hold on. If constraint four is the exact opposite of the first three,", "tokens": [51205, 3802, 11, 1699, 11, 1797, 322, 13, 759, 25534, 1451, 307, 264, 1900, 6182, 295, 264, 700, 1045, 11, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12984624151456153, "compression_ratio": 1.875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617380214911659e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 82144, "start": 843.1400000000001, "end": 846.2800000000001, "text": " then the system is in a total deadlock.", "tokens": [51450, 550, 264, 1185, 307, 294, 257, 3217, 3116, 4102, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12984624151456153, "compression_ratio": 1.875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617380214911659e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 84628, "start": 846.28, "end": 852.0, "text": " Because if the first three algorithms say a transaction is safe, the fourth algorithm says it's fraudulent.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 264, 700, 1045, 14642, 584, 257, 14425, 307, 3273, 11, 264, 6409, 9284, 1619, 309, 311, 14560, 23405, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 84628, "start": 852.06, "end": 854.86, "text": " And if the fourth says it's safe, the first three say it's fraudulent.", "tokens": [50654, 400, 498, 264, 6409, 1619, 309, 311, 3273, 11, 264, 700, 1045, 584, 309, 311, 14560, 23405, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 84628, "start": 855.04, "end": 857.62, "text": " It is worse than deadlocked. It is mathematically infeasible.", "tokens": [50803, 467, 307, 5324, 813, 3116, 4102, 292, 13, 467, 307, 44003, 1536, 68, 296, 964, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 84628, "start": 857.74, "end": 862.56, "text": " There is not a single action in the universe that can satisfy all four constraints simultaneously.", "tokens": [50938, 821, 307, 406, 257, 2167, 3069, 294, 264, 6445, 300, 393, 19319, 439, 1451, 18491, 16561, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 84628, "start": 862.86, "end": 864.76, "text": " The system is just completely paralyzed.", "tokens": [51194, 440, 1185, 307, 445, 2584, 41919, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 84628, "start": 865.26, "end": 865.74, "text": " Paralyzed.", "tokens": [51314, 3457, 5222, 11312, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 84628, "start": 865.8, "end": 869.5, "text": " Okay, so clearly the dashboard monitoring this system should be flashing red.", "tokens": [51341, 1033, 11, 370, 4448, 264, 18342, 11028, 341, 1185, 820, 312, 31049, 2182, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 84628, "start": 869.9, "end": 872.1, "text": " The diversity score should tell us the system is broken.", "tokens": [51546, 440, 8811, 6175, 820, 980, 505, 264, 1185, 307, 5463, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 84628, "start": 872.42, "end": 873.36, "text": " Well, let's run the math.", "tokens": [51672, 1042, 11, 718, 311, 1190, 264, 5221, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401218021617217, "compression_ratio": 1.8098360655737704, "no_speech_prob": 1.554973489380218e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 87336, "start": 873.36, "end": 878.82, "text": " When you calculate the correlation between the three redundant constraints, they are identical.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 8873, 264, 20009, 1296, 264, 1045, 40997, 18491, 11, 436, 366, 14800, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 87336, "start": 879.12, "end": 881.38, "text": " So they give a positive correlation of plus one.", "tokens": [50653, 407, 436, 976, 257, 3353, 20009, 295, 1804, 472, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 87336, "start": 881.64, "end": 882.74, "text": " Right, because they always agree.", "tokens": [50779, 1779, 11, 570, 436, 1009, 3986, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 87336, "start": 883.12, "end": 886.74, "text": " But when you calculate the correlation between those three and the fourth constraint,", "tokens": [50853, 583, 562, 291, 8873, 264, 20009, 1296, 729, 1045, 293, 264, 6409, 25534, 11, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 87336, "start": 887.08, "end": 891.16, "text": " they are exact opposites, giving a negative correlation of minus one.", "tokens": [51051, 436, 366, 1900, 4665, 3324, 11, 2902, 257, 3671, 20009, 295, 3175, 472, 13, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 87336, "start": 891.26, "end": 893.28, "text": " I see where this is going and I hate it.", "tokens": [51260, 286, 536, 689, 341, 307, 516, 293, 286, 4700, 309, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 87336, "start": 893.48, "end": 898.04, "text": " When you average them all out, the positive correlation contributed by the redundancy", "tokens": [51371, 1133, 291, 4274, 552, 439, 484, 11, 264, 3353, 20009, 18434, 538, 264, 27830, 6717, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213930840585746, "compression_ratio": 1.9870689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747622169285825e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 89804, "start": 898.04, "end": 904.06, "text": " and the negative correlation contributed by the genuine conflict perfectly cancel each other out.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 264, 3671, 20009, 18434, 538, 264, 16699, 6596, 6239, 10373, 1184, 661, 484, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18108770009633657, "compression_ratio": 1.6130653266331658, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507009096261346e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 89804, "start": 904.12, "end": 904.76, "text": " Oh my gosh.", "tokens": [50669, 876, 452, 6502, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18108770009633657, "compression_ratio": 1.6130653266331658, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507009096261346e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 89804, "start": 904.8199999999999, "end": 906.52, "text": " The average correlation is zero.", "tokens": [50704, 440, 4274, 20009, 307, 4018, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18108770009633657, "compression_ratio": 1.6130653266331658, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507009096261346e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 89804, "start": 906.7199999999999, "end": 912.66, "text": " And when the correlation is zero, the diversity score DG outputs a perfect four out of four.", "tokens": [50799, 400, 562, 264, 20009, 307, 4018, 11, 264, 8811, 6175, 413, 38, 23930, 257, 2176, 1451, 484, 295, 1451, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18108770009633657, "compression_ratio": 1.6130653266331658, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507009096261346e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 89804, "start": 912.9, "end": 913.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51108, 7587, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18108770009633657, "compression_ratio": 1.6130653266331658, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507009096261346e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 89804, "start": 913.52, "end": 917.4, "text": " It reports a maximally diverse, perfectly healthy population of constraints.", "tokens": [51139, 467, 7122, 257, 5138, 379, 9521, 11, 6239, 4627, 4415, 295, 18491, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18108770009633657, "compression_ratio": 1.6130653266331658, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507009096261346e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 91740, "start": 917.4, "end": 922.72, "text": " So if I'm the bank manager looking at my dashboard, the math tells me my security is perfect.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 286, 478, 264, 3765, 6598, 1237, 412, 452, 18342, 11, 264, 5221, 5112, 385, 452, 3825, 307, 2176, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14421394543770033, "compression_ratio": 1.548936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776662966148324e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 91740, "start": 923.26, "end": 928.76, "text": " When in reality, my security guards are literally fighting each other and stopping every single transaction.", "tokens": [50658, 1133, 294, 4103, 11, 452, 3825, 17652, 366, 3736, 5237, 1184, 661, 293, 12767, 633, 2167, 14425, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14421394543770033, "compression_ratio": 1.548936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776662966148324e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 91740, "start": 929.3, "end": 930.92, "text": " This is exactly the pathology.", "tokens": [50960, 639, 307, 2293, 264, 3100, 1793, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14421394543770033, "compression_ratio": 1.548936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776662966148324e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 91740, "start": 931.38, "end": 938.86, "text": " It proves that population health cannot be read off a single scalar score when redundancy and conflict are simultaneously present.", "tokens": [51064, 467, 25019, 300, 4415, 1585, 2644, 312, 1401, 766, 257, 2167, 39684, 6175, 562, 27830, 6717, 293, 6596, 366, 16561, 1974, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14421394543770033, "compression_ratio": 1.548936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776662966148324e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 93886, "start": 938.86, "end": 947.72, "text": " That is just, it's wild to think how many systems might be operating under that exact illusion right now.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 445, 11, 309, 311, 4868, 281, 519, 577, 867, 3652, 1062, 312, 7447, 833, 300, 1900, 18854, 558, 586, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 93886, "start": 948.0600000000001, "end": 949.92, "text": " So how do you actually fix it?", "tokens": [50825, 407, 577, 360, 291, 767, 3191, 309, 30, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 93886, "start": 950.3000000000001, "end": 953.58, "text": " How do you see through the mask if the math itself is lying to you?", "tokens": [50937, 1012, 360, 291, 536, 807, 264, 6094, 498, 264, 5221, 2564, 307, 8493, 281, 291, 30, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 93886, "start": 953.84, "end": 955.34, "text": " You have to separate the concepts.", "tokens": [51114, 509, 362, 281, 4994, 264, 10392, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 93886, "start": 955.76, "end": 961.32, "text": " You must check feasibility, whether the rules can actually exist together separately from diversity.", "tokens": [51210, 509, 1633, 1520, 21781, 2841, 11, 1968, 264, 4474, 393, 767, 2514, 1214, 14759, 490, 8811, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 93886, "start": 961.46, "end": 963.16, "text": " Right, you can't just smush them into one number.", "tokens": [51495, 1779, 11, 291, 393, 380, 445, 899, 1498, 552, 666, 472, 1230, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 93886, "start": 963.16, "end": 968.66, "text": " And the text introduces a brilliant diagnostic tool called the marginal diversity contribution.", "tokens": [51580, 400, 264, 2487, 31472, 257, 10248, 27897, 2290, 1219, 264, 16885, 8811, 13150, 13, 51855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14949262142181396, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.579842701972256e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 96886, "start": 969.72, "end": 970.24, "text": " How does that work?", "tokens": [50408, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 30, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 96886, "start": 970.4, "end": 977.38, "text": " Instead of looking at the whole score at once, you systematically remove one constraint at a time and see how the total score changes.", "tokens": [50442, 7156, 295, 1237, 412, 264, 1379, 6175, 412, 1564, 11, 291, 39531, 4159, 472, 25534, 412, 257, 565, 293, 536, 577, 264, 3217, 6175, 2962, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 96886, "start": 977.46, "end": 978.4, "text": " So you stress test it.", "tokens": [50795, 407, 291, 4244, 1500, 309, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 96886, "start": 978.64, "end": 978.94, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50854, 1079, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 96886, "start": 979.42, "end": 988.6, "text": " If you fire one of your redundant security guards, the measure diversity of the remaining group actually goes up because you removed a source of mathematical redundancy.", "tokens": [50893, 759, 291, 2610, 472, 295, 428, 40997, 3825, 17652, 11, 264, 3481, 8811, 295, 264, 8877, 1594, 767, 1709, 493, 570, 291, 7261, 257, 4009, 295, 18894, 27830, 6717, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 96886, "start": 988.6, "end": 993.6800000000001, "text": " Oh, because they were dragging the true score down by just being identical to the other guys.", "tokens": [51352, 876, 11, 570, 436, 645, 24385, 264, 2074, 6175, 760, 538, 445, 885, 14800, 281, 264, 661, 1074, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 96886, "start": 993.86, "end": 994.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51615, 7587, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 96886, "start": 995.0, "end": 997.48, "text": " The text calls this an invasive constraint.", "tokens": [51672, 440, 2487, 5498, 341, 364, 30894, 25534, 13, 51796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16867971420288086, "compression_ratio": 1.6972789115646258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106481824663342e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 99748, "start": 997.48, "end": 1004.1800000000001, "text": " It looks like it is adding to the population, but it is actively suppressing the real diversity of the network.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1542, 411, 309, 307, 5127, 281, 264, 4415, 11, 457, 309, 307, 13022, 1003, 18605, 264, 957, 8811, 295, 264, 3209, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08441046925334188, "compression_ratio": 1.6355932203389831, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941724514964337e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 99748, "start": 1004.4, "end": 1005.26, "text": " That makes total sense.", "tokens": [50711, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08441046925334188, "compression_ratio": 1.6355932203389831, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941724514964337e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 99748, "start": 1005.38, "end": 1017.28, "text": " By checking the marginal contribution, stress testing the system by dropping rules one by one, you can mathematically identify exactly which constraints are genuinely contributing coverage and which ones are just giving you a false sense of security.", "tokens": [50760, 3146, 8568, 264, 16885, 13150, 11, 4244, 4997, 264, 1185, 538, 13601, 4474, 472, 538, 472, 11, 291, 393, 44003, 5876, 2293, 597, 18491, 366, 17839, 19270, 9645, 293, 597, 2306, 366, 445, 2902, 291, 257, 7908, 2020, 295, 3825, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08441046925334188, "compression_ratio": 1.6355932203389831, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941724514964337e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 101728, "start": 1017.28, "end": 1019.06, "text": " That is incredible.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 4651, 13, 50454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 101728, "start": 1019.06, "end": 1027.98, "text": " Okay, so we've got our distinguishability boundaries, we've got our constraint rules, and we know how to check if those rules are actually working or just masking a failure.", "tokens": [50454, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 600, 658, 527, 20206, 2310, 13180, 11, 321, 600, 658, 527, 25534, 4474, 11, 293, 321, 458, 577, 281, 1520, 498, 729, 4474, 366, 767, 1364, 420, 445, 31226, 257, 7763, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 101728, "start": 1028.24, "end": 1028.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50913, 1779, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 101728, "start": 1028.92, "end": 1032.22, "text": " But what happens when the rules inevitably do break?", "tokens": [50947, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 264, 4474, 28171, 360, 1821, 30, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 101728, "start": 1032.76, "end": 1033.5, "text": " Because they will.", "tokens": [51139, 1436, 436, 486, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 101728, "start": 1033.84, "end": 1036.0, "text": " What happens when those distinctions are lost?", "tokens": [51193, 708, 2314, 562, 729, 1483, 49798, 366, 2731, 30, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 101728, "start": 1036.56, "end": 1039.26, "text": " That brings us to entropy and the shrinking future.", "tokens": [51329, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 30867, 293, 264, 41684, 2027, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2341903854202438, "compression_ratio": 1.592274678111588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837686201224498e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 103926, "start": 1039.26, "end": 1044.26, "text": " Yes, infliction makes it very clear this isn't just about a messy bedroom getting messier.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 9922, 4105, 1669, 309, 588, 1850, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 466, 257, 16191, 11211, 1242, 2082, 811, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11782659530639648, "compression_ratio": 1.589090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609864967124464e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 103926, "start": 1044.36, "end": 1045.02, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50620, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11782659530639648, "compression_ratio": 1.589090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609864967124464e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 103926, "start": 1045.24, "end": 1047.8, "text": " It is far more consequential than just disorder.", "tokens": [50664, 467, 307, 1400, 544, 7242, 2549, 813, 445, 13399, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11782659530639648, "compression_ratio": 1.589090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609864967124464e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 103926, "start": 1048.58, "end": 1059.06, "text": " The text actually evaluates five different candidates for what entropy might mean in the context of persistence, but it tightly links two of them, Shannon entropy and representational entropy.", "tokens": [50831, 440, 2487, 767, 6133, 1024, 1732, 819, 11255, 337, 437, 30867, 1062, 914, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 37617, 11, 457, 309, 21952, 6123, 732, 295, 552, 11, 28974, 30867, 293, 2906, 1478, 30867, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11782659530639648, "compression_ratio": 1.589090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609864967124464e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 103926, "start": 1059.4, "end": 1062.92, "text": " Break those down for me because entropy is one of those words people throw around a lot.", "tokens": [51372, 16925, 729, 760, 337, 385, 570, 30867, 307, 472, 295, 729, 2283, 561, 3507, 926, 257, 688, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11782659530639648, "compression_ratio": 1.589090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609864967124464e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 106292, "start": 1062.92, "end": 1068.02, "text": " Sure. Shannon entropy measures the distinction or separation between different categories.", "tokens": [50365, 4894, 13, 28974, 30867, 8000, 264, 16844, 420, 14634, 1296, 819, 10479, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 106292, "start": 1068.68, "end": 1070.16, "text": " It is a measure of surprise.", "tokens": [50653, 467, 307, 257, 3481, 295, 6365, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 106292, "start": 1070.44, "end": 1071.04, "text": " Okay, surprise.", "tokens": [50741, 1033, 11, 6365, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 106292, "start": 1071.04, "end": 1079.94, "text": " If I pull a random crayon from a box of 128, you are more surprised by the specific color than if I pulled from a box of 8.", "tokens": [50771, 759, 286, 2235, 257, 4974, 33073, 266, 490, 257, 2424, 295, 29810, 11, 291, 366, 544, 6100, 538, 264, 2685, 2017, 813, 498, 286, 7373, 490, 257, 2424, 295, 1649, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 106292, "start": 1080.5600000000002, "end": 1084.04, "text": " The Shannon entropy is higher because there are more distinct choices.", "tokens": [51247, 440, 28974, 30867, 307, 2946, 570, 456, 366, 544, 10644, 7994, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 106292, "start": 1084.92, "end": 1085.5600000000002, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [51465, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 106292, "start": 1085.92, "end": 1090.1000000000001, "text": " Representational entropy, however, measures the multiplicity within a single category.", "tokens": [51515, 19945, 1478, 30867, 11, 4461, 11, 8000, 264, 17596, 507, 1951, 257, 2167, 7719, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1571662379246132, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169132005527942e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 109010, "start": 1090.1, "end": 1094.82, "text": " How many underlying states were compressed into that one label?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 867, 14217, 4368, 645, 30353, 666, 300, 472, 7645, 30, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 109010, "start": 1095.34, "end": 1096.36, "text": " So back to the sand.", "tokens": [50627, 407, 646, 281, 264, 4932, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 109010, "start": 1096.9199999999998, "end": 1101.7199999999998, "text": " If I only have the one desert sand crayon, the representational entropy is massive.", "tokens": [50706, 759, 286, 787, 362, 264, 472, 11029, 4932, 33073, 266, 11, 264, 2906, 1478, 30867, 307, 5994, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 109010, "start": 1101.8999999999999, "end": 1102.3799999999999, "text": " Massive.", "tokens": [50955, 10482, 488, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 109010, "start": 1102.48, "end": 1106.1399999999999, "text": " Because there are millions of unique grains hiding behind that one label.", "tokens": [50984, 1436, 456, 366, 6803, 295, 3845, 22908, 10596, 2261, 300, 472, 7645, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 109010, "start": 1106.3, "end": 1106.82, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51175, 7587, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 109010, "start": 1107.32, "end": 1110.02, "text": " They are duels of the exact same partition structure.", "tokens": [51226, 814, 366, 1581, 1625, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 24808, 3877, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 109010, "start": 1110.3, "end": 1115.76, "text": " If you refine your categories, if you get that bigger box of crayons, your Shannon entropy goes up because you have more choices.", "tokens": [51375, 759, 291, 33906, 428, 10479, 11, 498, 291, 483, 300, 3801, 2424, 295, 33073, 892, 11, 428, 28974, 30867, 1709, 493, 570, 291, 362, 544, 7994, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13669097095454505, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108365284694172e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 111576, "start": 1115.76, "end": 1121.56, "text": " But your representational entropy goes down because there are fewer unknown variables hiding behind each choice.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 428, 2906, 1478, 30867, 1709, 760, 570, 456, 366, 13366, 9841, 9102, 10596, 2261, 1184, 3922, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13820529806202855, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189483785343905e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 111576, "start": 1121.66, "end": 1122.64, "text": " You've got it perfectly.", "tokens": [50660, 509, 600, 658, 309, 6239, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13820529806202855, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189483785343905e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 111576, "start": 1123.12, "end": 1123.34, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50733, 1033, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13820529806202855, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189483785343905e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 111576, "start": 1123.52, "end": 1131.82, "text": " And this leads to how fliction reinterprets the second law of thermodynamics, which, you know, usually states that the entropy of a closed system always increases.", "tokens": [50753, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 577, 932, 4105, 319, 5106, 3712, 1373, 264, 1150, 2101, 295, 8810, 35483, 11, 597, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2673, 4368, 300, 264, 30867, 295, 257, 5395, 1185, 1009, 8637, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13820529806202855, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189483785343905e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 111576, "start": 1132.24, "end": 1136.98, "text": " But they write, entropy increase is the shadow cast by distinction loss.", "tokens": [51189, 583, 436, 2464, 11, 30867, 3488, 307, 264, 8576, 4193, 538, 16844, 4470, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13820529806202855, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189483785343905e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 113698, "start": 1136.98, "end": 1139.58, "text": " It is a profound rephrasing.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 319, 44598, 3349, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1661736806233724, "compression_ratio": 1.5869565217391304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106099743826152e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 113698, "start": 1140.54, "end": 1150.04, "text": " When a system's ability to distinguish states coarsens, when it loses the ability to tell two things apart, whether through damage, noise, or decay entropy increases.", "tokens": [50543, 1133, 257, 1185, 311, 3485, 281, 20206, 4368, 598, 685, 694, 11, 562, 309, 18293, 264, 3485, 281, 980, 732, 721, 4936, 11, 1968, 807, 4344, 11, 5658, 11, 420, 21039, 30867, 8637, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1661736806233724, "compression_ratio": 1.5869565217391304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106099743826152e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 113698, "start": 1150.42, "end": 1150.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51037, 1779, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1661736806233724, "compression_ratio": 1.5869565217391304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106099743826152e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 113698, "start": 1150.8, "end": 1157.8, "text": " But the crucial link here, the real world consequence, is what the text calls effective reachability contraction.", "tokens": [51056, 583, 264, 11462, 2113, 510, 11, 264, 957, 1002, 18326, 11, 307, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 4942, 2524, 2310, 37372, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1661736806233724, "compression_ratio": 1.5869565217391304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106099743826152e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 113698, "start": 1158.08, "end": 1158.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51420, 1779, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1661736806233724, "compression_ratio": 1.5869565217391304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106099743826152e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 113698, "start": 1158.3, "end": 1160.08, "text": " This is the idea of the shrinking future.", "tokens": [51431, 639, 307, 264, 1558, 295, 264, 41684, 2027, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1661736806233724, "compression_ratio": 1.5869565217391304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106099743826152e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 116008, "start": 1160.08, "end": 1160.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 116008, "start": 1160.98, "end": 1166.8799999999999, "text": " When your distinction structure coarsens, the set of effective reachable states in your future shrinks.", "tokens": [50410, 1133, 428, 16844, 3877, 598, 685, 694, 11, 264, 992, 295, 4942, 2524, 712, 4368, 294, 428, 2027, 9884, 16431, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 116008, "start": 1167.24, "end": 1167.86, "text": " Give me an example.", "tokens": [50723, 5303, 385, 364, 1365, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 116008, "start": 1168.1999999999998, "end": 1180.8999999999999, "text": " If you are driving and your vision blurs so you can no longer tell the difference between a green light and a red light, the safe future states that depended on you making that distinction collapse, you effectively have fewer viable futures.", "tokens": [50771, 759, 291, 366, 4840, 293, 428, 5201, 888, 2156, 370, 291, 393, 572, 2854, 980, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 3092, 1442, 293, 257, 2182, 1442, 11, 264, 3273, 2027, 4368, 300, 1367, 3502, 322, 291, 1455, 300, 16844, 15584, 11, 291, 8659, 362, 13366, 22024, 26071, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 116008, "start": 1181.1799999999998, "end": 1181.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51420, 1033, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 116008, "start": 1181.56, "end": 1182.76, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [51439, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 116008, "start": 1182.8799999999999, "end": 1186.24, "text": " And I actually have to push back a little here to make sure I'm grasping the metaphysics of this.", "tokens": [51505, 400, 286, 767, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 257, 707, 510, 281, 652, 988, 286, 478, 29444, 3381, 264, 30946, 41732, 295, 341, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 116008, "start": 1186.26, "end": 1186.6, "text": " Please do.", "tokens": [51674, 2555, 360, 13, 51691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09655622733655826, "compression_ratio": 1.6913183279742765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897986273451624e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 118660, "start": 1186.6, "end": 1194.8999999999999, "text": " Just because I close my eyes, right, and can't distinguish between the green light and the red light, that doesn't mean the intersection physically disappears from the universe.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 570, 286, 1998, 452, 2575, 11, 558, 11, 293, 393, 380, 20206, 1296, 264, 3092, 1442, 293, 264, 2182, 1442, 11, 300, 1177, 380, 914, 264, 15236, 9762, 25527, 490, 264, 6445, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 118660, "start": 1195.1399999999999, "end": 1195.76, "text": " No, it doesn't.", "tokens": [50792, 883, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 118660, "start": 1195.84, "end": 1196.8799999999999, "text": " The asphalt is still there.", "tokens": [50827, 440, 46076, 307, 920, 456, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 118660, "start": 1196.9599999999998, "end": 1197.86, "text": " The cars are still there.", "tokens": [50883, 440, 5163, 366, 920, 456, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 118660, "start": 1198.3999999999999, "end": 1201.6, "text": " Why does losing information mean I lose physical options?", "tokens": [50955, 1545, 775, 7027, 1589, 914, 286, 3624, 4001, 3956, 30, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 118660, "start": 1201.8999999999999, "end": 1210.9199999999998, "text": " It is a vital question, and it cuts right to the core of what the text calls the cybernetic hypothesis or distinction-dependent controllability.", "tokens": [51130, 467, 307, 257, 11707, 1168, 11, 293, 309, 9992, 558, 281, 264, 4965, 295, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 264, 13411, 77, 3532, 17291, 420, 16844, 12, 36763, 317, 45159, 2310, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 118660, "start": 1211.2199999999998, "end": 1211.4399999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51596, 1033, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11925103642919042, "compression_ratio": 1.695167286245353, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145486218654745e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 121144, "start": 1211.44, "end": 1213.02, "text": " You are absolutely right.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 3122, 558, 13, 50444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 121144, "start": 1213.22, "end": 1217.6000000000001, "text": " The physical intersection still exists in the universe independently of your perception.", "tokens": [50454, 440, 4001, 15236, 920, 8198, 294, 264, 6445, 21761, 295, 428, 12860, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 121144, "start": 1218.5800000000002, "end": 1228.1000000000001, "text": " But if your executable actions are inextricably tied to your representation, then losing the distinction deletes the path for you as an agent.", "tokens": [50722, 583, 498, 428, 7568, 712, 5909, 366, 294, 3828, 1341, 1188, 9601, 281, 428, 10290, 11, 550, 7027, 264, 16844, 1103, 37996, 264, 3100, 337, 291, 382, 364, 9461, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 121144, "start": 1228.4, "end": 1229.16, "text": " Let's ground this.", "tokens": [51213, 961, 311, 2727, 341, 13, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 121144, "start": 1229.3200000000002, "end": 1231.06, "text": " Give me a concrete, real-world example.", "tokens": [51259, 5303, 385, 257, 9859, 11, 957, 12, 13217, 1365, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 121144, "start": 1231.3600000000001, "end": 1234.16, "text": " Think of a robotic arm on a high-speed assembly line.", "tokens": [51361, 6557, 295, 257, 30468, 3726, 322, 257, 1090, 12, 22746, 12103, 1622, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 121144, "start": 1234.28, "end": 1234.52, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51507, 1033, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13355960237218978, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300905736714607e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 123452, "start": 1234.52, "end": 1242.92, "text": " It is programmed with a specific rule. Pick up a part only if the camera detects a perfect square. If it detects a rectangle, ignore it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 31092, 365, 257, 2685, 4978, 13, 14129, 493, 257, 644, 787, 498, 264, 2799, 5531, 82, 257, 2176, 3732, 13, 759, 309, 5531, 82, 257, 21930, 11, 11200, 309, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07305458458987149, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356270998287279e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 123452, "start": 1243.04, "end": 1246.0, "text": " Got it. Square means pick it up. Rectangle means ignore.", "tokens": [50791, 5803, 309, 13, 16463, 1355, 1888, 309, 493, 13, 497, 557, 7846, 1355, 11200, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07305458458987149, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356270998287279e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 123452, "start": 1246.32, "end": 1253.52, "text": " Over time, the camera lens degrades. It loses resolution. It loses the distinction between a square and a slightly elongated rectangle.", "tokens": [50955, 4886, 565, 11, 264, 2799, 6765, 368, 22626, 13, 467, 18293, 8669, 13, 467, 18293, 264, 16844, 1296, 257, 3732, 293, 257, 4748, 40786, 770, 21930, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07305458458987149, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356270998287279e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 123452, "start": 1254.2, "end": 1254.74, "text": " It gets blurry.", "tokens": [51349, 467, 2170, 37644, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07305458458987149, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356270998287279e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 125474, "start": 1254.74, "end": 1259.52, "text": " Now, the physical square part is still moving down the conveyor belt. It exists in the universe.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 264, 4001, 3732, 644, 307, 920, 2684, 760, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 13, 467, 8198, 294, 264, 6445, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943011442820232, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.1917456998615803e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 125474, "start": 1260.34, "end": 1266.4, "text": " But the robot's action, the physical movement of the mechanical arm, is triggered by the distinction.", "tokens": [50645, 583, 264, 7881, 311, 3069, 11, 264, 4001, 3963, 295, 264, 12070, 3726, 11, 307, 21710, 538, 264, 16844, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943011442820232, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.1917456998615803e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 125474, "start": 1266.6, "end": 1267.2, "text": " Without the distinction.", "tokens": [50958, 9129, 264, 16844, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943011442820232, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.1917456998615803e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 125474, "start": 1267.38, "end": 1269.02, "text": " The physical action cannot be executed.", "tokens": [50997, 440, 4001, 3069, 2644, 312, 17577, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943011442820232, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.1917456998615803e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 125474, "start": 1269.2, "end": 1270.64, "text": " It's just paralyzed by the blur.", "tokens": [51088, 467, 311, 445, 41919, 538, 264, 14257, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943011442820232, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.1917456998615803e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 127064, "start": 1270.64, "end": 1278.88, "text": " Exactly. The physical future where the arm successfully moves the square is effectively deleted from the robot's reachable future.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 4001, 2027, 689, 264, 3726, 10727, 6067, 264, 3732, 307, 8659, 22981, 490, 264, 7881, 311, 2524, 712, 2027, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18793873909192207, "compression_ratio": 1.7355769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967475380784026e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 127064, "start": 1279.0800000000002, "end": 1279.4, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50787, 3153, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18793873909192207, "compression_ratio": 1.7355769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967475380784026e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 127064, "start": 1279.8400000000001, "end": 1282.4, "text": " This is the entropy admissibility corollary.", "tokens": [50825, 639, 307, 264, 30867, 5910, 891, 2841, 1181, 1833, 822, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18793873909192207, "compression_ratio": 1.7355769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967475380784026e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 127064, "start": 1282.98, "end": 1287.7, "text": " Entropy production provably contracts your effective reachability unconditionally.", "tokens": [50982, 3951, 27514, 4265, 1439, 1188, 13952, 428, 4942, 2524, 2310, 34959, 15899, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18793873909192207, "compression_ratio": 1.7355769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967475380784026e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 127064, "start": 1288.2800000000002, "end": 1293.5, "text": " And it contracts your physical reachability if your physical actions depend on your distinctions.", "tokens": [51247, 400, 309, 13952, 428, 4001, 2524, 2310, 498, 428, 4001, 5909, 5672, 322, 428, 1483, 49798, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18793873909192207, "compression_ratio": 1.7355769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967475380784026e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 129350, "start": 1293.5, "end": 1301.72, "text": " So, if my actions depend on what I can see, and I go blind to a difference, I literally lose the physical ability to act on that difference.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 452, 5909, 5672, 322, 437, 286, 393, 536, 11, 293, 286, 352, 6865, 281, 257, 2649, 11, 286, 3736, 3624, 264, 4001, 3485, 281, 605, 322, 300, 2649, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 129350, "start": 1301.94, "end": 1305.26, "text": " My physical future shrinks because my informational map shrank.", "tokens": [50787, 1222, 4001, 2027, 9884, 16431, 570, 452, 49391, 4471, 9884, 657, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 129350, "start": 1305.38, "end": 1305.76, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50959, 1079, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 129350, "start": 1306.24, "end": 1307.8, "text": " That is haunting. It really is.", "tokens": [51002, 663, 307, 44512, 13, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 129350, "start": 1307.86, "end": 1310.06, "text": " It is. Because entropy is relentless.", "tokens": [51083, 467, 307, 13, 1436, 30867, 307, 46136, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 129350, "start": 1310.58, "end": 1314.5, "text": " It is constantly degrading sensors, breaking rules, and blurring distinctions.", "tokens": [51219, 467, 307, 6460, 24740, 278, 14840, 11, 7697, 4474, 11, 293, 14257, 2937, 1483, 49798, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 129350, "start": 1314.74, "end": 1316.28, "text": " Which brings up the obvious question, right?", "tokens": [51427, 3013, 5607, 493, 264, 6322, 1168, 11, 558, 30, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 129350, "start": 1316.34, "end": 1316.44, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51507, 865, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 129350, "start": 1316.5, "end": 1321.22, "text": " If entropy is constantly shrinking our reachable future, how do systems persist at all?", "tokens": [51515, 759, 30867, 307, 6460, 41684, 527, 2524, 712, 2027, 11, 577, 360, 3652, 13233, 412, 439, 30, 51751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15429913051544675, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.051939347602616e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 132122, "start": 1321.22, "end": 1325.44, "text": " Like, why hasn't civilization or biology just ground to a halt?", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 983, 6132, 380, 18036, 420, 14956, 445, 2727, 281, 257, 12479, 30, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 132122, "start": 1326.16, "end": 1329.6200000000001, "text": " Well, because systems don't just sit there and let entropy wash over them.", "tokens": [50612, 1042, 11, 570, 3652, 500, 380, 445, 1394, 456, 293, 718, 30867, 5675, 670, 552, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 132122, "start": 1329.8, "end": 1331.44, "text": " They actively fight back.", "tokens": [50794, 814, 13022, 2092, 646, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 132122, "start": 1331.92, "end": 1333.04, "text": " They repair themselves.", "tokens": [50900, 814, 10535, 2969, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 132122, "start": 1333.32, "end": 1333.6000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50970, 1079, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 132122, "start": 1334.14, "end": 1337.42, "text": " To understand survival, we have to look at how a system adapts.", "tokens": [51011, 1407, 1223, 12559, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 577, 257, 1185, 23169, 1373, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 132122, "start": 1337.66, "end": 1343.24, "text": " The text formally defines three levels of adaptation, and distinguishing them is absolutely crucial.", "tokens": [51187, 440, 2487, 25983, 23122, 1045, 4358, 295, 21549, 11, 293, 11365, 3807, 552, 307, 3122, 11462, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 132122, "start": 1343.4, "end": 1343.78, "text": " That's the rhythm.", "tokens": [51474, 663, 311, 264, 11801, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 132122, "start": 1343.92, "end": 1345.42, "text": " Level one is state update.", "tokens": [51500, 16872, 472, 307, 1785, 5623, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 132122, "start": 1345.84, "end": 1349.04, "text": " The system moves through its state space under an unchanging rule.", "tokens": [51596, 440, 1185, 6067, 807, 1080, 1785, 1901, 833, 364, 517, 27123, 4978, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17049407958984375, "compression_ratio": 1.6241379310344828, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738117390533105e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 134904, "start": 1349.04, "end": 1354.98, "text": " Like a train on a track. The train moves, the scenery changes, but the track itself doesn't change.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 257, 3847, 322, 257, 2837, 13, 440, 3847, 6067, 11, 264, 25805, 2962, 11, 457, 264, 2837, 2564, 1177, 380, 1319, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 134904, "start": 1355.32, "end": 1357.8, "text": " Precisely. Level two is parameter update.", "tokens": [50679, 48746, 736, 13, 16872, 732, 307, 13075, 5623, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 134904, "start": 1358.26, "end": 1363.08, "text": " The behavior changes, but only within the range expressible by a fixed family of rules.", "tokens": [50826, 440, 5223, 2962, 11, 457, 787, 1951, 264, 3613, 5109, 964, 538, 257, 6806, 1605, 295, 4474, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 134904, "start": 1363.42, "end": 1367.54, "text": " So, like a smart thermostat, it adapts its output based on the ambient temperature.", "tokens": [51084, 407, 11, 411, 257, 4069, 8810, 39036, 11, 309, 23169, 1373, 1080, 5598, 2361, 322, 264, 22997, 4292, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 134904, "start": 1368.02, "end": 1372.62, "text": " But its fundamental programming to regulate heat is static. It's still just a thermostat.", "tokens": [51314, 583, 1080, 8088, 9410, 281, 24475, 3738, 307, 13437, 13, 467, 311, 920, 445, 257, 8810, 39036, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 134904, "start": 1372.86, "end": 1374.8799999999999, "text": " Right. But level three is rule update.", "tokens": [51556, 1779, 13, 583, 1496, 1045, 307, 4978, 5623, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 134904, "start": 1375.18, "end": 1375.98, "text": " Okay. Level three.", "tokens": [51672, 1033, 13, 16872, 1045, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10206882770244892, "compression_ratio": 1.6702898550724639, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760848130751739e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 137598, "start": 1375.98, "end": 1380.56, "text": " This is where the mapping that governs future behavior is itself the object being modified.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 689, 264, 18350, 300, 1980, 82, 2027, 5223, 307, 2564, 264, 2657, 885, 15873, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16343036890029908, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.708209745529543e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 137598, "start": 1381.08, "end": 1382.2, "text": " This is true repair.", "tokens": [50620, 639, 307, 2074, 10535, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16343036890029908, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.708209745529543e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 137598, "start": 1382.58, "end": 1386.5, "text": " A system that merely moves or adjusts parameters isn't repairing anything.", "tokens": [50695, 316, 1185, 300, 17003, 6067, 420, 4369, 82, 9834, 1943, 380, 46158, 1340, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16343036890029908, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.708209745529543e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 137598, "start": 1386.66, "end": 1387.8600000000001, "text": " It's just running its program.", "tokens": [50899, 467, 311, 445, 2614, 1080, 1461, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16343036890029908, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.708209745529543e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 137598, "start": 1388.34, "end": 1390.92, "text": " Repair requires modifying the operator itself.", "tokens": [50983, 3696, 1246, 7029, 42626, 264, 12973, 2564, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16343036890029908, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.708209745529543e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 137598, "start": 1391.24, "end": 1395.72, "text": " And this leads to how we even judge if a system has survived damage.", "tokens": [51128, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 577, 321, 754, 6995, 498, 257, 1185, 575, 14433, 4344, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16343036890029908, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.708209745529543e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 139572, "start": 1395.72, "end": 1398.48, "text": " Because it's not always obvious.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 309, 311, 406, 1009, 6322, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 139572, "start": 1399.0, "end": 1403.6000000000001, "text": " The text outlines an equivalence hierarchy to measure survival.", "tokens": [50529, 440, 2487, 40125, 364, 9052, 655, 22333, 281, 3481, 12559, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 139572, "start": 1404.28, "end": 1406.0, "text": " First, you have state equivalent.", "tokens": [50793, 2386, 11, 291, 362, 1785, 10344, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 139572, "start": 1406.3600000000001, "end": 1409.26, "text": " Two systems occupy the exact same state right now.", "tokens": [50897, 4453, 3652, 30645, 264, 1900, 912, 1785, 558, 586, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 139572, "start": 1409.3600000000001, "end": 1409.6000000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51047, 1033, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 139572, "start": 1409.84, "end": 1411.08, "text": " Then structural equivalent.", "tokens": [51071, 1396, 15067, 10344, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 139572, "start": 1411.28, "end": 1412.78, "text": " Their underlying architectures agree.", "tokens": [51143, 6710, 14217, 6331, 1303, 3986, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 139572, "start": 1413.24, "end": 1414.64, "text": " Then behavioral equivalent.", "tokens": [51241, 1396, 19124, 10344, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 139572, "start": 1414.82, "end": 1417.34, "text": " You can't tell their input-output behavior apart.", "tokens": [51320, 509, 393, 380, 980, 641, 4846, 12, 346, 2582, 5223, 4936, 13, 51446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 139572, "start": 1417.5, "end": 1422.4, "text": " But the text argues that all of these are terribly insufficient for measuring true resilience, right?", "tokens": [51454, 583, 264, 2487, 38218, 300, 439, 295, 613, 366, 22903, 41709, 337, 13389, 2074, 19980, 11, 558, 30, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 139572, "start": 1422.6200000000001, "end": 1425.0, "text": " Because they only look at a snapshot in time.", "tokens": [51710, 1436, 436, 787, 574, 412, 257, 30163, 294, 565, 13, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18968529079271398, "compression_ratio": 1.6748251748251748, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779821247076774e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 142500, "start": 1425.0, "end": 1425.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1281573904885186, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.393870153847121e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 142500, "start": 1425.72, "end": 1431.94, "text": " I mean, two coastal cities might look completely identical in their state, their structural layout, and their current economic behavior.", "tokens": [50401, 286, 914, 11, 732, 25050, 6486, 1062, 574, 2584, 14800, 294, 641, 1785, 11, 641, 15067, 13333, 11, 293, 641, 2190, 4836, 5223, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1281573904885186, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.393870153847121e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 142500, "start": 1432.06, "end": 1432.42, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50718, 1079, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1281573904885186, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.393870153847121e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 142500, "start": 1432.78, "end": 1442.9, "text": " But if one city recently slashed its budget by firing its emergency planners and throwing out its municipal archives, it has fundamentally lost its ability to recover from the next hurricane.", "tokens": [50754, 583, 498, 472, 2307, 3938, 1061, 12219, 1080, 4706, 538, 16045, 1080, 7473, 49674, 293, 10238, 484, 1080, 27177, 25607, 11, 309, 575, 17879, 2731, 1080, 3485, 281, 8114, 490, 264, 958, 27136, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1281573904885186, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.393870153847121e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 144290, "start": 1442.9, "end": 1443.5, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 144290, "start": 1443.88, "end": 1445.2, "text": " Even though it looks fine right now.", "tokens": [50414, 2754, 1673, 309, 1542, 2489, 558, 586, 13, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 144290, "start": 1445.94, "end": 1449.3600000000001, "text": " That is why the highest, most vital level is regenerative equivalent.", "tokens": [50517, 663, 307, 983, 264, 6343, 11, 881, 11707, 1496, 307, 26358, 1166, 10344, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 144290, "start": 1449.5, "end": 1450.4, "text": " Regenerative equivalent.", "tokens": [50695, 4791, 7971, 1166, 10344, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 144290, "start": 1450.8600000000001, "end": 1455.8600000000001, "text": " Meaning, they possess the operator ecology to recreate future capacities after damage.", "tokens": [50763, 19948, 11, 436, 17490, 264, 12973, 39683, 281, 25833, 2027, 39396, 934, 4344, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 144290, "start": 1456.24, "end": 1456.5400000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51032, 1079, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 144290, "start": 1457.26, "end": 1458.96, "text": " It's not about what you're doing now.", "tokens": [51083, 467, 311, 406, 466, 437, 291, 434, 884, 586, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 144290, "start": 1459.0600000000002, "end": 1462.1200000000001, "text": " It's about what you retain the capacity to build again tomorrow.", "tokens": [51173, 467, 311, 466, 437, 291, 18340, 264, 6042, 281, 1322, 797, 4153, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19290766605111057, "compression_ratio": 1.6028708133971292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552456020418882e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 146212, "start": 1462.12, "end": 1465.52, "text": " And this brings us to the concept of operator ecologies.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 3410, 295, 12973, 11437, 6204, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2183912992477417, "compression_ratio": 1.3111111111111111, "no_speech_prob": 2.027601827755965e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 146212, "start": 1466.3999999999999, "end": 1469.8799999999999, "text": " An operator ecology is not just a list of tools in a toolbox.", "tokens": [50579, 1107, 12973, 39683, 307, 406, 445, 257, 1329, 295, 3873, 294, 257, 44593, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2183912992477417, "compression_ratio": 1.3111111111111111, "no_speech_prob": 2.027601827755965e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 146988, "start": 1469.88, "end": 1473.3600000000001, "text": " No, it is a deeply interconnected constraint network.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 309, 307, 257, 8760, 36611, 25534, 3209, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18305622100830077, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2181993655084886e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 146988, "start": 1473.94, "end": 1478.7600000000002, "text": " It is the dependency structure that determines which tools can actually be used and when.", "tokens": [50568, 467, 307, 264, 33621, 3877, 300, 24799, 597, 3873, 393, 767, 312, 1143, 293, 562, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18305622100830077, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2181993655084886e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 146988, "start": 1479.2600000000002, "end": 1483.2600000000002, "text": " And within this complex network, you have what Fliction calls keystone operators.", "tokens": [50834, 400, 1951, 341, 3997, 3209, 11, 291, 362, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 2141, 11243, 19077, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18305622100830077, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 2.2181993655084886e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 148326, "start": 1483.26, "end": 1486.72, "text": " Like a keystone species in a biological ecosystem.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 257, 2141, 11243, 6172, 294, 257, 13910, 11311, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 148326, "start": 1487.02, "end": 1491.86, "text": " Like if you remove the wolves from Yellowstone, the entire ecosystem collapses, even the flow of the rivers.", "tokens": [50553, 1743, 498, 291, 4159, 264, 30404, 490, 17550, 11243, 11, 264, 2302, 11311, 48765, 11, 754, 264, 3095, 295, 264, 18361, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 148326, "start": 1492.12, "end": 1494.42, "text": " The exact same logic applies to systems.", "tokens": [50808, 440, 1900, 912, 9952, 13165, 281, 3652, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 148326, "start": 1494.8799999999999, "end": 1502.62, "text": " A keystone operator might be invoked very rarely, but its loss disconnects massive, sprawling regions of future state spaces.", "tokens": [50946, 316, 2141, 11243, 12973, 1062, 312, 1048, 9511, 588, 13752, 11, 457, 1080, 4470, 14299, 82, 5994, 11, 22734, 1688, 10682, 295, 2027, 1785, 7673, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 148326, "start": 1502.9, "end": 1506.06, "text": " The text calls this generative keystone impact.", "tokens": [51347, 440, 2487, 5498, 341, 1337, 1166, 2141, 11243, 2712, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 148326, "start": 1506.34, "end": 1507.92, "text": " Give me an example of that in human society.", "tokens": [51519, 5303, 385, 364, 1365, 295, 300, 294, 1952, 4086, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 148326, "start": 1508.22, "end": 1512.16, "text": " Think of a highly specialized apprenticeship program in a manufacturing sector.", "tokens": [51613, 6557, 295, 257, 5405, 19813, 47070, 1461, 294, 257, 11096, 6977, 13, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10066183826379609, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 151216, "start": 1512.16, "end": 1514.0, "text": " It might only graduate 10 people a year.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1062, 787, 8080, 1266, 561, 257, 1064, 13, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 151216, "start": 1514.3600000000001, "end": 1515.88, "text": " It looks inefficient on a spreadsheet.", "tokens": [50475, 467, 1542, 43495, 322, 257, 27733, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 151216, "start": 1516.02, "end": 1516.1200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50558, 1779, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 151216, "start": 1516.26, "end": 1517.38, "text": " Some accountant wants to cut it.", "tokens": [50570, 2188, 43898, 2738, 281, 1723, 309, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 151216, "start": 1517.64, "end": 1526.1000000000001, "text": " But if you lose it 50 years later, every single industry that depended on those esoteric skills, from aerospace to infrastructure collapses.", "tokens": [50639, 583, 498, 291, 3624, 309, 2625, 924, 1780, 11, 633, 2167, 3518, 300, 1367, 3502, 322, 729, 785, 21585, 299, 3942, 11, 490, 46817, 281, 6896, 48765, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 151216, "start": 1526.4, "end": 1533.24, "text": " But keeping all these extra operators around, keeping training programs and archives and redundant systems running, that's expensive.", "tokens": [51077, 583, 5145, 439, 613, 2857, 19077, 926, 11, 5145, 3097, 4268, 293, 25607, 293, 40997, 3652, 2614, 11, 300, 311, 5124, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 151216, "start": 1533.3600000000001, "end": 1535.0600000000002, "text": " It drags down quarterly profits.", "tokens": [51425, 467, 5286, 82, 760, 38633, 17982, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 151216, "start": 1535.3200000000002, "end": 1536.1200000000001, "text": " Yes, it does.", "tokens": [51523, 1079, 11, 309, 775, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11823487962995256, "compression_ratio": 1.5638297872340425, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492051864783197e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 153612, "start": 1536.12, "end": 1542.84, "text": " Which leads to what I think is one of the most brutal theorems in the entire text, the anti-alignment theorem.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 6689, 281, 437, 286, 519, 307, 472, 295, 264, 881, 17878, 10299, 2592, 294, 264, 2302, 2487, 11, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306181958926622, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045773650746886e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 153612, "start": 1543.04, "end": 1548.02, "text": " It is a stark mathematical reality that pushes back against modern optimization trends.", "tokens": [50711, 467, 307, 257, 17417, 18894, 4103, 300, 21020, 646, 1970, 4363, 19618, 13892, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306181958926622, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045773650746886e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 153612, "start": 1548.12, "end": 1548.8799999999999, "text": " Let's talk about it.", "tokens": [50965, 961, 311, 751, 466, 309, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306181958926622, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045773650746886e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 153612, "start": 1549.12, "end": 1555.9399999999998, "text": " The anti-alignment theorem states that there is a fundamental tension between enacting an operator efficiently and repairing it later.", "tokens": [51015, 440, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 4368, 300, 456, 307, 257, 8088, 8980, 1296, 25909, 278, 364, 12973, 19621, 293, 46158, 309, 1780, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306181958926622, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045773650746886e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 153612, "start": 1556.1599999999999, "end": 1557.52, "text": " Wait, let me make sure I'm getting this.", "tokens": [51367, 3802, 11, 718, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 1242, 341, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306181958926622, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045773650746886e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 155752, "start": 1557.52, "end": 1570.6, "text": " By striving for absolute efficiency like a massive tech company firing its entire documentation department or a global supply chain operating on just-in-time manufacturing with zero warehouse buffer.", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 36582, 337, 8236, 10493, 411, 257, 5994, 7553, 2237, 16045, 1080, 2302, 14333, 5882, 420, 257, 4338, 5847, 5021, 7447, 322, 445, 12, 259, 12, 3766, 11096, 365, 4018, 22244, 21762, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13380439353711676, "compression_ratio": 1.4807692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674038672877644e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 155752, "start": 1570.86, "end": 1571.22, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51032, 1079, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13380439353711676, "compression_ratio": 1.4807692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674038672877644e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 155752, "start": 1571.56, "end": 1575.84, "text": " You are mathematically guaranteeing you won't be able to fix the system when it inevitably breaks.", "tokens": [51067, 509, 366, 44003, 10815, 278, 291, 1582, 380, 312, 1075, 281, 3191, 264, 1185, 562, 309, 28171, 9857, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13380439353711676, "compression_ratio": 1.4807692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674038672877644e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 155752, "start": 1575.98, "end": 1576.24, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51288, 1079, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13380439353711676, "compression_ratio": 1.4807692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674038672877644e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 157624, "start": 1576.24, "end": 1584.42, "text": " The text mathematically proves that the minimal trace required to efficiently run an operator is generically the worst possible trace for repairing it later.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 44003, 25019, 300, 264, 13206, 13508, 4739, 281, 19621, 1190, 364, 12973, 307, 1337, 984, 264, 5855, 1944, 13508, 337, 46158, 309, 1780, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16988462056869116, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482859777928628e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 157624, "start": 1584.74, "end": 1585.74, "text": " That is huge.", "tokens": [50790, 663, 307, 2603, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16988462056869116, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482859777928628e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 157624, "start": 1585.98, "end": 1587.14, "text": " That explains so much.", "tokens": [50852, 663, 13948, 370, 709, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16988462056869116, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482859777928628e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 157624, "start": 1587.38, "end": 1590.04, "text": " It explains so much of modern systemic fragility.", "tokens": [50922, 467, 13948, 370, 709, 295, 4363, 23789, 9241, 1140, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16988462056869116, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482859777928628e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 157624, "start": 1590.72, "end": 1594.42, "text": " Efficient compression systematically destroys repairability.", "tokens": [51089, 462, 7816, 19355, 39531, 36714, 10535, 2310, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16988462056869116, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482859777928628e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 157624, "start": 1594.6200000000001, "end": 1597.28, "text": " Because you're throwing out the instructions to save weight.", "tokens": [51284, 1436, 291, 434, 10238, 484, 264, 9415, 281, 3155, 3364, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16988462056869116, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482859777928628e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 159728, "start": 1597.28, "end": 1597.92, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10271384980943468, "compression_ratio": 1.5444015444015444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147411962570303e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 159728, "start": 1598.34, "end": 1614.18, "text": " When you optimize a process to run with the absolute minimum number of steps and the least amount of stored memory, you are discarding the historical trace, the context, and the redundant pathways that you will desperately need to diagnose and reconstruct the system when it fails.", "tokens": [50418, 1133, 291, 19719, 257, 1399, 281, 1190, 365, 264, 8236, 7285, 1230, 295, 4439, 293, 264, 1935, 2372, 295, 12187, 4675, 11, 291, 366, 31597, 278, 264, 8584, 13508, 11, 264, 4319, 11, 293, 264, 40997, 22988, 300, 291, 486, 23726, 643, 281, 36238, 293, 31499, 264, 1185, 562, 309, 18199, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10271384980943468, "compression_ratio": 1.5444015444015444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147411962570303e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 159728, "start": 1614.28, "end": 1616.1399999999999, "text": " You're optimizing yourself into a corner.", "tokens": [51215, 509, 434, 40425, 1803, 666, 257, 4538, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10271384980943468, "compression_ratio": 1.5444015444015444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147411962570303e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 159728, "start": 1616.58, "end": 1619.58, "text": " I feel like every CEO on Earth needs to read that theorem.", "tokens": [51330, 286, 841, 411, 633, 9282, 322, 4755, 2203, 281, 1401, 300, 20904, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10271384980943468, "compression_ratio": 1.5444015444015444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147411962570303e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 159728, "start": 1619.8, "end": 1620.04, "text": " Truly.", "tokens": [51491, 43548, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10271384980943468, "compression_ratio": 1.5444015444015444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147411962570303e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 162004, "start": 1620.04, "end": 1629.26, "text": " To really ground this idea of how ecologies fail and how true repair actually works, the text provides this brilliant historical example.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 534, 2727, 341, 1558, 295, 577, 11437, 6204, 3061, 293, 577, 2074, 10535, 767, 1985, 11, 264, 2487, 6417, 341, 10248, 8584, 1365, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 162004, "start": 1629.3999999999999, "end": 1632.06, "text": " It's a master class in separating three things we usually confuse.", "tokens": [50833, 467, 311, 257, 4505, 1508, 294, 29279, 1045, 721, 321, 2673, 28584, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 162004, "start": 1632.46, "end": 1632.78, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50986, 1079, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 162004, "start": 1632.8799999999999, "end": 1636.04, "text": " It uses the story of the classical pianist Paul Wittgenstein.", "tokens": [51007, 467, 4960, 264, 1657, 295, 264, 13735, 32198, 468, 4552, 343, 593, 1766, 9089, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 162004, "start": 1636.48, "end": 1642.0, "text": " Let's walk through this because it perfectly illustrates the difference between fixing a problem and generating a new capacity.", "tokens": [51187, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 341, 570, 309, 6239, 41718, 264, 2649, 1296, 19442, 257, 1154, 293, 17746, 257, 777, 6042, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 162004, "start": 1642.28, "end": 1644.02, "text": " It is a beautiful application of the theory.", "tokens": [51477, 467, 307, 257, 2238, 3861, 295, 264, 5261, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 162004, "start": 1644.36, "end": 1646.94, "text": " The text outlines three stages of failure and repair.", "tokens": [51581, 440, 2487, 40125, 1045, 10232, 295, 7763, 293, 10535, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 162004, "start": 1647.76, "end": 1648.96, "text": " Stage one is misalignment.", "tokens": [51751, 25907, 472, 307, 3346, 304, 41134, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11016899744669596, "compression_ratio": 1.6773162939297124, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897472783315327e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 164896, "start": 1648.96, "end": 1650.3400000000001, "text": " Okay, misalignment.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 3346, 304, 41134, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14543596903483072, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837643917339771e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 164896, "start": 1650.72, "end": 1658.0, "text": " Imagine a piano where the keys are mechanically relabeled or restrung so that high pitch is on the left and low pitch is on the right.", "tokens": [50453, 11739, 257, 9211, 689, 264, 9317, 366, 4236, 984, 1039, 18657, 292, 420, 1472, 81, 1063, 370, 300, 1090, 7293, 307, 322, 264, 1411, 293, 2295, 7293, 307, 322, 264, 558, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14543596903483072, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837643917339771e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 164896, "start": 1658.14, "end": 1659.32, "text": " Okay, so it's a backwards piano.", "tokens": [50824, 1033, 11, 370, 309, 311, 257, 12204, 9211, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14543596903483072, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837643917339771e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 164896, "start": 1659.58, "end": 1661.1200000000001, "text": " Every physical key is still there.", "tokens": [50896, 2048, 4001, 2141, 307, 920, 456, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14543596903483072, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837643917339771e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 164896, "start": 1661.48, "end": 1667.14, "text": " The pianist's physical ability to move their fingers, their operator repertoire, is completely intact.", "tokens": [50991, 440, 32198, 468, 311, 4001, 3485, 281, 1286, 641, 7350, 11, 641, 12973, 49604, 11, 307, 2584, 23493, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14543596903483072, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837643917339771e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 164896, "start": 1667.46, "end": 1673.3600000000001, "text": " But the correspondence between their trained, internalized movements and the physical target space is broken.", "tokens": [51290, 583, 264, 38135, 1296, 641, 8895, 11, 6920, 1602, 9981, 293, 264, 4001, 3779, 1901, 307, 5463, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14543596903483072, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837643917339771e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 167336, "start": 1673.36, "end": 1679.86, "text": " So they know exactly how to play, like a Chopin nocturne, but the instrument has just changed underneath them.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 458, 2293, 577, 281, 862, 11, 411, 257, 25615, 259, 572, 349, 374, 716, 11, 457, 264, 7198, 575, 445, 3105, 7223, 552, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 167336, "start": 1679.9599999999998, "end": 1680.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50695, 7587, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 167336, "start": 1680.6399999999999, "end": 1681.4399999999998, "text": " That's misalignment.", "tokens": [50729, 663, 311, 3346, 304, 41134, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 167336, "start": 1681.86, "end": 1684.08, "text": " It can be fixed by just retuning the piano.", "tokens": [50790, 467, 393, 312, 6806, 538, 445, 1533, 37726, 264, 9211, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 167336, "start": 1684.4599999999998, "end": 1684.9799999999998, "text": " Simple enough.", "tokens": [50920, 21532, 1547, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 167336, "start": 1685.3, "end": 1687.06, "text": " But stage two is extinction.", "tokens": [50962, 583, 3233, 732, 307, 33163, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 167336, "start": 1687.4599999999998, "end": 1689.6999999999998, "text": " And this is where Paul Wittgenstein comes in.", "tokens": [51070, 400, 341, 307, 689, 4552, 343, 593, 1766, 9089, 1487, 294, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 167336, "start": 1689.78, "end": 1692.82, "text": " He was a concert pianist who lost his right arm in the First World War.", "tokens": [51186, 634, 390, 257, 8543, 32198, 468, 567, 2731, 702, 558, 3726, 294, 264, 2386, 3937, 3630, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 167336, "start": 1692.9399999999998, "end": 1693.2199999999998, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51344, 3153, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16321185884021577, "compression_ratio": 1.4686192468619246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214529498058018e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 169322, "start": 1693.22, "end": 1697.0, "text": " This is extinction in the precise mathematical definition of the text.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 33163, 294, 264, 13600, 18894, 7123, 295, 264, 2487, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11516849890999172, "compression_ratio": 1.4093959731543624, "no_speech_prob": 1.2884960026021686e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 169322, "start": 1697.0, "end": 1706.42, "text": " An entire sub-repertoire of his trained operators, every single movement, every chord requiring two hands, became permanently inexecutable.", "tokens": [50554, 1107, 2302, 1422, 12, 265, 610, 47144, 295, 702, 8895, 19077, 11, 633, 2167, 3963, 11, 633, 14137, 24165, 732, 2377, 11, 3062, 24042, 29961, 3045, 32148, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11516849890999172, "compression_ratio": 1.4093959731543624, "no_speech_prob": 1.2884960026021686e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 170642, "start": 1706.42, "end": 1711.02, "text": " A massive fraction of his accessible state space simply ceased to exist.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 5994, 14135, 295, 702, 9515, 1785, 1901, 2935, 49917, 281, 2514, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 170642, "start": 1711.4, "end": 1713.6000000000001, "text": " It's not just mislabeled like the backwards piano.", "tokens": [50614, 467, 311, 406, 445, 3346, 75, 18657, 292, 411, 264, 12204, 9211, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 170642, "start": 1713.8400000000001, "end": 1715.8400000000001, "text": " It's physically permanently gone.", "tokens": [50736, 467, 311, 9762, 24042, 2780, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 170642, "start": 1716.0800000000002, "end": 1719.02, "text": " You can't just retune the instrument to fix a missing arm.", "tokens": [50848, 509, 393, 380, 445, 1533, 2613, 264, 7198, 281, 3191, 257, 5361, 3726, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 170642, "start": 1719.16, "end": 1720.28, "text": " Which leads to stage three.", "tokens": [51002, 3013, 6689, 281, 3233, 1045, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 170642, "start": 1721.42, "end": 1721.8600000000001, "text": " Regeneration.", "tokens": [51115, 4791, 268, 5053, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 170642, "start": 1722.66, "end": 1730.8000000000002, "text": " Wittgenstein didn't just try to use his left hand to awkwardly patch over two-handed pieces, you know, clumsily jumping across the keys to hit the missing notes.", "tokens": [51177, 343, 593, 1766, 9089, 994, 380, 445, 853, 281, 764, 702, 1411, 1011, 281, 11411, 356, 9972, 670, 732, 12, 25407, 3755, 11, 291, 458, 11, 596, 8099, 953, 11233, 2108, 264, 9317, 281, 2045, 264, 5361, 5570, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 170642, "start": 1730.94, "end": 1733.3600000000001, "text": " Which is what a lot of systems would try to do, just patch it.", "tokens": [51591, 3013, 307, 437, 257, 688, 295, 3652, 576, 853, 281, 360, 11, 445, 9972, 309, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 170642, "start": 1733.5, "end": 1733.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51719, 1779, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 170642, "start": 1734.16, "end": 1735.44, "text": " But he didn't do that.", "tokens": [51752, 583, 415, 994, 380, 360, 300, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11046145667492503, "compression_ratio": 1.6548387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.106965213937272e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 173544, "start": 1735.44, "end": 1745.3400000000001, "text": " He commissioned an entirely new body of concert repertoire for the left hand alone, from master composers like Maurice Ravel, Sergei Prokofiev, and Benjamin Britten.", "tokens": [50365, 634, 32372, 364, 7696, 777, 1772, 295, 8543, 49604, 337, 264, 1411, 1011, 3312, 11, 490, 4505, 43872, 411, 49041, 7591, 779, 11, 18885, 72, 1705, 74, 2670, 9037, 11, 293, 22231, 1603, 2987, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 173544, "start": 1745.6000000000001, "end": 1747.8400000000001, "text": " He didn't just ask for a repair to the old system.", "tokens": [50873, 634, 994, 380, 445, 1029, 337, 257, 10535, 281, 264, 1331, 1185, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 173544, "start": 1748.1200000000001, "end": 1749.44, "text": " He built a brand new ecology.", "tokens": [50999, 634, 3094, 257, 3360, 777, 39683, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 173544, "start": 1750.22, "end": 1750.7, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51104, 48746, 736, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 173544, "start": 1751.14, "end": 1754.16, "text": " The Ravel Piano Concerto for the left hand isn't just a band-aid.", "tokens": [51150, 440, 7591, 779, 430, 6254, 18200, 13098, 337, 264, 1411, 1011, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 4116, 12, 17810, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 173544, "start": 1754.38, "end": 1760.8400000000001, "text": " It created new pedagogical traditions, new compositional vocabularies, specifically suited to the new constraint.", "tokens": [51312, 467, 2942, 777, 5670, 31599, 804, 15643, 11, 777, 10199, 2628, 2329, 455, 1040, 530, 11, 4682, 24736, 281, 264, 777, 25534, 13, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 173544, "start": 1761.04, "end": 1763.74, "text": " It generated further techniques that didn't even exist before.", "tokens": [51645, 467, 10833, 3052, 7512, 300, 994, 380, 754, 2514, 949, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041378336628591, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0605175551913213e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 176374, "start": 1763.74, "end": 1764.1200000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724449396133423, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941720178155647e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 176374, "start": 1764.32, "end": 1766.36, "text": " It was a true regenerative operator.", "tokens": [50394, 467, 390, 257, 2074, 26358, 1166, 12973, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724449396133423, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941720178155647e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 176374, "start": 1766.96, "end": 1772.46, "text": " It increased the ecology's future capacity to produce art, rather than merely patching a past loss.", "tokens": [50526, 467, 6505, 264, 39683, 311, 2027, 6042, 281, 5258, 1523, 11, 2831, 813, 17003, 9972, 278, 257, 1791, 4470, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724449396133423, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941720178155647e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 176374, "start": 1772.64, "end": 1776.5, "text": " It's such a powerful example of what Level 3 repair actually looks like.", "tokens": [50810, 467, 311, 1270, 257, 4005, 1365, 295, 437, 16872, 805, 10535, 767, 1542, 411, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724449396133423, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941720178155647e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 176374, "start": 1777.06, "end": 1787.3, "text": " But, you know, despite all these regenerative ecologies, despite all our best efforts to build Ravel Concertos, eventually, a system hits a hard limit where repair is simply impossible.", "tokens": [51031, 583, 11, 291, 458, 11, 7228, 439, 613, 26358, 1166, 11437, 6204, 11, 7228, 439, 527, 1151, 6484, 281, 1322, 7591, 779, 18200, 45152, 11, 4728, 11, 257, 1185, 8664, 257, 1152, 4948, 689, 10535, 307, 2935, 6243, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724449396133423, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941720178155647e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 178730, "start": 1787.3, "end": 1788.3, "text": " It is inevitable.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 21451, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 178730, "start": 1788.6399999999999, "end": 1792.78, "text": " This brings us to what Flictioning calls the restorability boundaries.", "tokens": [50432, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 437, 3235, 4105, 278, 5498, 264, 46594, 2310, 13180, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 178730, "start": 1793.1599999999999, "end": 1797.6599999999999, "text": " And I found it fascinating that this boundary isn't just one monolithic brick wall.", "tokens": [50658, 400, 286, 1352, 309, 10343, 300, 341, 12866, 1943, 380, 445, 472, 1108, 42878, 16725, 2929, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 178730, "start": 1797.9199999999998, "end": 1801.36, "text": " It's actually four distinct failure modes.", "tokens": [50896, 467, 311, 767, 1451, 10644, 7763, 14068, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 178730, "start": 1801.82, "end": 1806.1399999999999, "text": " But before we even get to the four modes, the text puts up a gatekeeper.", "tokens": [51091, 583, 949, 321, 754, 483, 281, 264, 1451, 14068, 11, 264, 2487, 8137, 493, 257, 8539, 23083, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 178730, "start": 1806.52, "end": 1808.6399999999999, "text": " It calls it the architecture gate.", "tokens": [51326, 467, 5498, 309, 264, 9482, 8539, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 178730, "start": 1808.98, "end": 1809.28, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51449, 1033, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 178730, "start": 1809.4199999999998, "end": 1810.36, "text": " The architecture gate.", "tokens": [51471, 440, 9482, 8539, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20789044836293097, "compression_ratio": 1.6073059360730593, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250535631370024e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 181036, "start": 1810.36, "end": 1814.8999999999999, "text": " It makes a crucial distinction between an inferential boundary and an ontological boundary.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1669, 257, 11462, 16844, 1296, 364, 13596, 2549, 12866, 293, 364, 6592, 4383, 12866, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1551892107183283, "compression_ratio": 1.6345381526104417, "no_speech_prob": 2.0276126697776897e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 181036, "start": 1814.8999999999999, "end": 1817.6, "text": " Break those down, because that sounds like heavy philosophy.", "tokens": [50592, 16925, 729, 760, 11, 570, 300, 3263, 411, 4676, 10675, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1551892107183283, "compression_ratio": 1.6345381526104417, "no_speech_prob": 2.0276126697776897e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 181036, "start": 1817.9399999999998, "end": 1824.52, "text": " An inferential boundary means the target you are trying to observe is technically representable within your current architecture.", "tokens": [50744, 1107, 13596, 2549, 12866, 1355, 264, 3779, 291, 366, 1382, 281, 11441, 307, 12120, 2906, 712, 1951, 428, 2190, 9482, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1551892107183283, "compression_ratio": 1.6345381526104417, "no_speech_prob": 2.0276126697776897e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 181036, "start": 1824.76, "end": 1830.06, "text": " You just can't fix it right now because of noise or lacking data or signal degradation.", "tokens": [51085, 509, 445, 393, 380, 3191, 309, 558, 586, 570, 295, 5658, 420, 20889, 1412, 420, 6358, 40519, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1551892107183283, "compression_ratio": 1.6345381526104417, "no_speech_prob": 2.0276126697776897e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 181036, "start": 1830.1799999999998, "end": 1831.6399999999999, "text": " I think so it's possible, just hard.", "tokens": [51356, 286, 519, 370, 309, 311, 1944, 11, 445, 1152, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1551892107183283, "compression_ratio": 1.6345381526104417, "no_speech_prob": 2.0276126697776897e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 183164, "start": 1831.64, "end": 1832.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 183164, "start": 1832.66, "end": 1839.5600000000002, "text": " But an ontological boundary means your architecture itself is fundamentally mathematically incapable of representing the observation.", "tokens": [50416, 583, 364, 6592, 4383, 12866, 1355, 428, 9482, 2564, 307, 17879, 44003, 44174, 295, 13460, 264, 14816, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 183164, "start": 1840.3000000000002, "end": 1843.66, "text": " No amount of data, no amount of signal boosting will help.", "tokens": [50798, 883, 2372, 295, 1412, 11, 572, 2372, 295, 6358, 43117, 486, 854, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 183164, "start": 1844.0600000000002, "end": 1848.2, "text": " The text uses two awesome astronomy examples here that really clarify this.", "tokens": [50986, 440, 2487, 4960, 732, 3476, 37844, 5110, 510, 300, 534, 17594, 341, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 183164, "start": 1848.88, "end": 1854.8000000000002, "text": " The first is Newtonian mechanics trying to explain the weird orbit of the planet Mercury.", "tokens": [51227, 440, 700, 307, 19541, 952, 12939, 1382, 281, 2903, 264, 3657, 13991, 295, 264, 5054, 31780, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 183164, "start": 1855.1200000000001, "end": 1855.42, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51539, 1079, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 183164, "start": 1855.6000000000001, "end": 1858.6200000000001, "text": " The anomalous precession of Mercury's perihelion.", "tokens": [51563, 440, 24769, 11553, 659, 29881, 295, 31780, 311, 680, 4247, 338, 313, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1840847705272918, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106039028504493e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 185862, "start": 1858.62, "end": 1864.52, "text": " For decades, Newtonian astronomers tried every conceivable repair within their architectural framework.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 7878, 11, 19541, 952, 43151, 3031, 633, 10413, 34376, 10535, 1951, 641, 26621, 8388, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 185862, "start": 1864.6599999999999, "end": 1866.1, "text": " They're just throwing everything at it.", "tokens": [50667, 814, 434, 445, 10238, 1203, 412, 309, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 185862, "start": 1866.2199999999998, "end": 1868.6599999999999, "text": " They hypothesized hidden planets pulling on mercury.", "tokens": [50745, 814, 14276, 1602, 7633, 15126, 8407, 322, 33307, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 185862, "start": 1868.8999999999999, "end": 1870.7199999999998, "text": " They hypothesized atmospheric drag.", "tokens": [50879, 814, 14276, 1602, 28854, 5286, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 185862, "start": 1870.9799999999998, "end": 1875.9399999999998, "text": " They even hypothesized the sun was slightly oblate, but the residual air wouldn't go away.", "tokens": [50983, 814, 754, 14276, 1602, 264, 3295, 390, 4748, 1111, 17593, 11, 457, 264, 27980, 1988, 2759, 380, 352, 1314, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 185862, "start": 1876.36, "end": 1877.78, "text": " Because it was an ontological boundary.", "tokens": [51252, 1436, 309, 390, 364, 6592, 4383, 12866, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 185862, "start": 1877.9399999999998, "end": 1882.9399999999998, "text": " No parameter choice, no new data point in Newtonian mechanics could explain it.", "tokens": [51331, 883, 13075, 3922, 11, 572, 777, 1412, 935, 294, 19541, 952, 12939, 727, 2903, 309, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 185862, "start": 1883.04, "end": 1883.3999999999999, "text": " No.", "tokens": [51586, 883, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15802501937718066, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182101874444911e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 188340, "start": 1883.4, "end": 1890.22, "text": " It required Albert Einstein and general relativity to expand the architecture itself to include the curvature of space-time.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 4739, 20812, 23486, 293, 2674, 45675, 281, 5268, 264, 9482, 2564, 281, 4090, 264, 37638, 295, 1901, 12, 3766, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 188340, "start": 1890.3600000000001, "end": 1890.6200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50713, 7587, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 188340, "start": 1890.8000000000002, "end": 1899.26, "text": " So contrast that with the paper by Bannock that the text cites where astronomers tried to reconstruct the age of the absolute oldest stars in the Milky Way galaxy.", "tokens": [50735, 407, 8712, 300, 365, 264, 3035, 538, 363, 969, 1560, 300, 264, 2487, 269, 3324, 689, 43151, 3031, 281, 31499, 264, 3205, 295, 264, 8236, 14026, 6105, 294, 264, 38465, 9558, 17639, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 188340, "start": 1899.38, "end": 1899.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51164, 1779, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 188340, "start": 1899.6000000000001, "end": 1901.0, "text": " The sub-giant stars.", "tokens": [51175, 440, 1422, 12, 70, 5798, 6105, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 188340, "start": 1901.24, "end": 1901.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51257, 1779, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 188340, "start": 1901.5, "end": 1902.5, "text": " They hit a noise floor.", "tokens": [51270, 814, 2045, 257, 5658, 4123, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 188340, "start": 1903.1000000000001, "end": 1905.68, "text": " The data just got too fuzzy to tell the exact age.", "tokens": [51350, 440, 1412, 445, 658, 886, 34710, 281, 980, 264, 1900, 3205, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 188340, "start": 1905.88, "end": 1907.68, "text": " That is an inferential boundary.", "tokens": [51489, 663, 307, 364, 13596, 2549, 12866, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1894742591040475, "compression_ratio": 1.5770609318996416, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689034915654989e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 190768, "start": 1907.68, "end": 1911.48, "text": " So the architecture of measuring stellar age works perfectly well.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 9482, 295, 13389, 42333, 3205, 1985, 6239, 731, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12656593322753906, "compression_ratio": 1.5893536121673004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878980851897651e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 190768, "start": 1911.96, "end": 1915.54, "text": " They just hit the physical limit of their instrument's ability to gather clear light.", "tokens": [50579, 814, 445, 2045, 264, 4001, 4948, 295, 641, 7198, 311, 3485, 281, 5448, 1850, 1442, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12656593322753906, "compression_ratio": 1.5893536121673004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878980851897651e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 190768, "start": 1915.7, "end": 1916.1200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50766, 7587, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12656593322753906, "compression_ratio": 1.5893536121673004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878980851897651e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 190768, "start": 1916.9, "end": 1925.16, "text": " Knowing which gate you are facing is critical because applying in-architecture fixes to an out-of-architecture problem is a recipe for endless, useless repair.", "tokens": [50826, 25499, 597, 8539, 291, 366, 7170, 307, 4924, 570, 9275, 294, 12, 1178, 5739, 540, 32539, 281, 364, 484, 12, 2670, 12, 1178, 5739, 540, 1154, 307, 257, 6782, 337, 16144, 11, 14115, 10535, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12656593322753906, "compression_ratio": 1.5893536121673004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878980851897651e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 190768, "start": 1925.76, "end": 1930.1200000000001, "text": " You can look for a hidden planet near Mercury for a thousand years and never find it.", "tokens": [51269, 509, 393, 574, 337, 257, 7633, 5054, 2651, 31780, 337, 257, 4714, 924, 293, 1128, 915, 309, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12656593322753906, "compression_ratio": 1.5893536121673004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878980851897651e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 190768, "start": 1930.3600000000001, "end": 1930.92, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51499, 48746, 736, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12656593322753906, "compression_ratio": 1.5893536121673004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878980851897651e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 193092, "start": 1930.92, "end": 1931.4, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 193092, "start": 1931.7, "end": 1941.9, "text": " Now, assuming we are past the architecture gate, assuming the problem is theoretically fixable within our framework, the text defines the signal diagnosis repair continuation chain.", "tokens": [50404, 823, 11, 11926, 321, 366, 1791, 264, 9482, 8539, 11, 11926, 264, 1154, 307, 29400, 3191, 712, 1951, 527, 8388, 11, 264, 2487, 23122, 264, 6358, 15217, 10535, 29357, 5021, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 193092, "start": 1942.04, "end": 1942.3600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50921, 1079, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 193092, "start": 1942.5600000000002, "end": 1942.74, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50947, 1033, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 193092, "start": 1942.76, "end": 1946.1000000000001, "text": " Let's turn this into a story so we can actually visualize these four failures.", "tokens": [50957, 961, 311, 1261, 341, 666, 257, 1657, 370, 321, 393, 767, 23273, 613, 1451, 20774, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 193092, "start": 1946.54, "end": 1949.42, "text": " Let's say we have a massive state-of-the-art hospital.", "tokens": [51146, 961, 311, 584, 321, 362, 257, 5994, 1785, 12, 2670, 12, 3322, 12, 446, 4530, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 193092, "start": 1949.94, "end": 1950.68, "text": " A storm hits.", "tokens": [51316, 316, 7679, 8664, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 193092, "start": 1950.78, "end": 1950.98, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [51358, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 193092, "start": 1951.02, "end": 1952.48, "text": " And the main power grid goes down.", "tokens": [51370, 400, 264, 2135, 1347, 10748, 1709, 760, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1632887704031808, "compression_ratio": 1.556, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122614512174675e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 195248, "start": 1952.48, "end": 1953.48, "text": " A perfect scenario.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 2176, 9005, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11789331796034327, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 195248, "start": 1954.0, "end": 1966.1200000000001, "text": " In this chain, a deviation, the power loss, has to generate a signal, the hospital system has to diagnose it, the system has to repair it locally, and then that repair has to continue globally to keep the patients alive.", "tokens": [50441, 682, 341, 5021, 11, 257, 25163, 11, 264, 1347, 4470, 11, 575, 281, 8460, 257, 6358, 11, 264, 4530, 1185, 575, 281, 36238, 309, 11, 264, 1185, 575, 281, 10535, 309, 16143, 11, 293, 550, 300, 10535, 575, 281, 2354, 18958, 281, 1066, 264, 4209, 5465, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11789331796034327, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 195248, "start": 1966.48, "end": 1969.1, "text": " And this chain gives us the four failure modes.", "tokens": [51065, 400, 341, 5021, 2709, 505, 264, 1451, 7763, 14068, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11789331796034327, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 195248, "start": 1969.66, "end": 1972.56, "text": " Mode number one, the expiatory gap.", "tokens": [51224, 20500, 1230, 472, 11, 264, 1278, 72, 4745, 7417, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11789331796034327, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 195248, "start": 1972.84, "end": 1974.22, "text": " Also known as throughput failure.", "tokens": [51383, 2743, 2570, 382, 44629, 7763, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11789331796034327, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 195248, "start": 1974.76, "end": 1978.4, "text": " This is when the signal is generated faster than the ecology can process it.", "tokens": [51479, 639, 307, 562, 264, 6358, 307, 10833, 4663, 813, 264, 39683, 393, 1399, 309, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11789331796034327, "compression_ratio": 1.7193675889328064, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 197840, "start": 1978.4, "end": 1986.18, "text": " The system's diagnostic rate, mathematically D's, exceeds its maximum processing rate, D max.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 311, 27897, 3314, 11, 44003, 413, 311, 11, 43305, 1080, 6674, 9007, 3314, 11, 413, 11469, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 197840, "start": 1986.2800000000002, "end": 1996.42, "text": " So in our hospital, the power goes out, and suddenly every single heart monitor, ventilator, and automated door sends an error alert to the central server at the exact same millisecond.", "tokens": [50759, 407, 294, 527, 4530, 11, 264, 1347, 1709, 484, 11, 293, 5800, 633, 2167, 1917, 6002, 11, 27498, 1639, 11, 293, 18473, 2853, 14790, 364, 6713, 9615, 281, 264, 5777, 7154, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 27940, 18882, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 197840, "start": 1996.48, "end": 1996.8200000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51269, 1079, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 197840, "start": 1996.9, "end": 1998.88, "text": " The server's completely overwhelmed and crashes.", "tokens": [51290, 440, 7154, 311, 2584, 19042, 293, 28642, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 197840, "start": 1999.22, "end": 2000.26, "text": " It's a throughput failure.", "tokens": [51406, 467, 311, 257, 44629, 7763, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 197840, "start": 2000.88, "end": 2004.48, "text": " And the text says, this is solvable by rate control, right?", "tokens": [51489, 400, 264, 2487, 1619, 11, 341, 307, 1404, 17915, 538, 3314, 1969, 11, 558, 30, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 197840, "start": 2004.5800000000002, "end": 2007.3600000000001, "text": " Just slow down the inputs, buffer them, you can catch up.", "tokens": [51674, 1449, 2964, 760, 264, 15743, 11, 21762, 552, 11, 291, 393, 3745, 493, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11434245513657391, "compression_ratio": 1.5620915032679739, "no_speech_prob": 2.04393489980359e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 200736, "start": 2007.36, "end": 2007.82, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 200736, "start": 2008.26, "end": 2014.6599999999999, "text": " You mute the low-priority door alarms so the server can process the life support alarms, but rate control will not fix the second mode.", "tokens": [50410, 509, 24523, 264, 2295, 12, 36391, 284, 507, 2853, 45039, 370, 264, 7154, 393, 1399, 264, 993, 1406, 45039, 11, 457, 3314, 1969, 486, 406, 3191, 264, 1150, 4391, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 200736, "start": 2014.84, "end": 2016.1999999999998, "text": " Which is diagnostic collapse.", "tokens": [50739, 3013, 307, 27897, 15584, 13, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 200736, "start": 2016.32, "end": 2018.06, "text": " Yes, a discriminability failure.", "tokens": [50813, 1079, 11, 257, 20828, 2310, 7763, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 200736, "start": 2018.56, "end": 2026.62, "text": " Here, the channel is fully active, it is processing the data perfectly, but the signal carries absolutely zero actual information about the root error.", "tokens": [50925, 1692, 11, 264, 2269, 307, 4498, 4967, 11, 309, 307, 9007, 264, 1412, 6239, 11, 457, 264, 6358, 16402, 3122, 4018, 3539, 1589, 466, 264, 5593, 6713, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 200736, "start": 2026.84, "end": 2028.6399999999999, "text": " So the mutual information drops to zero.", "tokens": [51339, 407, 264, 16917, 1589, 11438, 281, 4018, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 200736, "start": 2028.74, "end": 2028.9599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51434, 7587, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899436327875877, "compression_ratio": 1.646341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610518520198235e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 202896, "start": 2028.96, "end": 2037.16, "text": " So in the hospital, the alarms are ringing, the server is processing them, but every single alarm just says general fault 404.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 294, 264, 4530, 11, 264, 45039, 366, 18423, 11, 264, 7154, 307, 9007, 552, 11, 457, 633, 2167, 14183, 445, 1619, 2674, 7441, 3356, 19, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951638247515704, "compression_ratio": 1.470899470899471, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756361481325756e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 202896, "start": 2037.26, "end": 2037.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50780, 1779, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951638247515704, "compression_ratio": 1.470899470899471, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756361481325756e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 202896, "start": 2037.88, "end": 2042.3, "text": " It doesn't tell you if the problem is a blown fuse, a severed wire, or a flooded basement.", "tokens": [50811, 467, 1177, 380, 980, 291, 498, 264, 1154, 307, 257, 16479, 31328, 11, 257, 2802, 292, 6234, 11, 420, 257, 31594, 16893, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951638247515704, "compression_ratio": 1.470899470899471, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756361481325756e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 202896, "start": 2042.88, "end": 2045.26, "text": " You have plenty of signal, but you have no diagnosis.", "tokens": [51061, 509, 362, 7140, 295, 6358, 11, 457, 291, 362, 572, 15217, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951638247515704, "compression_ratio": 1.470899470899471, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756361481325756e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 204526, "start": 2045.26, "end": 2048.76, "text": " The Bannock star age example falls here, too.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 363, 969, 1560, 3543, 3205, 1365, 8804, 510, 11, 886, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 204526, "start": 2049.02, "end": 2051.7, "text": " The boundary isn't where the starlight disappears.", "tokens": [50553, 440, 12866, 1943, 380, 689, 264, 3543, 2764, 25527, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 204526, "start": 2052.24, "end": 2058.88, "text": " The boundary is where the starlight becomes mathematically indistinguishable from the noise, the reconstruction process itself.", "tokens": [50714, 440, 12866, 307, 689, 264, 3543, 2764, 3643, 44003, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 264, 5658, 11, 264, 31565, 1399, 2564, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 204526, "start": 2059.26, "end": 2061.46, "text": " The boundary is discriminability.", "tokens": [51065, 440, 12866, 307, 20828, 2310, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 204526, "start": 2061.88, "end": 2062.06, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51196, 1033, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 204526, "start": 2062.26, "end": 2064.5, "text": " Mode number three, repair deficit.", "tokens": [51215, 20500, 1230, 1045, 11, 10535, 22132, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 204526, "start": 2065.56, "end": 2066.82, "text": " This is operator failure.", "tokens": [51380, 639, 307, 12973, 7763, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 204526, "start": 2067.04, "end": 2067.14, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51454, 865, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 204526, "start": 2067.22, "end": 2072.84, "text": " You get the signal, you diagnose it perfectly, you know exactly what's wrong, but you have no executable operator to fix it.", "tokens": [51463, 509, 483, 264, 6358, 11, 291, 36238, 309, 6239, 11, 291, 458, 2293, 437, 311, 2085, 11, 457, 291, 362, 572, 7568, 712, 12973, 281, 3191, 309, 13, 51744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778605585512908, "compression_ratio": 1.7078651685393258, "no_speech_prob": 1.7208191252157667e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 207284, "start": 2072.84, "end": 2078.88, "text": " And here the text makes a beautiful distinction within this mode between a structural deficit and an energetic deficit.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 264, 2487, 1669, 257, 2238, 16844, 1951, 341, 4391, 1296, 257, 15067, 22132, 293, 364, 24935, 22132, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 207284, "start": 2079.2000000000003, "end": 2082.6000000000004, "text": " A structural deficit means the operator simply does not exist in your ecology.", "tokens": [50683, 316, 15067, 22132, 1355, 264, 12973, 2935, 775, 406, 2514, 294, 428, 39683, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 207284, "start": 2083.0, "end": 2087.92, "text": " So we know the backup generator has a cracked valve, but we literally don't own a wrench.", "tokens": [50873, 407, 321, 458, 264, 14807, 19265, 575, 257, 25140, 15294, 11, 457, 321, 3736, 500, 380, 1065, 257, 25406, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 207284, "start": 2088.26, "end": 2089.06, "text": " Structural deficit.", "tokens": [51136, 745, 1757, 1807, 22132, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 207284, "start": 2089.2200000000003, "end": 2089.5, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51184, 1079, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 207284, "start": 2089.9, "end": 2093.78, "text": " An energetic deficit, however, means the operator exists, but it cannot run.", "tokens": [51218, 1107, 24935, 22132, 11, 4461, 11, 1355, 264, 12973, 8198, 11, 457, 309, 2644, 1190, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 207284, "start": 2093.94, "end": 2097.2400000000002, "text": " We have the wrench, but the mechanic is too exhausted to turn it.", "tokens": [51420, 492, 362, 264, 25406, 11, 457, 264, 23860, 307, 886, 17992, 281, 1261, 309, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 207284, "start": 2097.6200000000003, "end": 2098.08, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51604, 7587, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14651463712964738, "compression_ratio": 1.7748091603053435, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 209808, "start": 2098.08, "end": 2103.56, "text": " The text points to the sodium-potassium pump in a biological cell to illustrate this.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 2793, 281, 264, 20265, 12, 17698, 27609, 5889, 294, 257, 13910, 2815, 281, 23221, 341, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11137447907374455, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659397807597623e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 209808, "start": 2104.14, "end": 2110.18, "text": " This pump maintains the neuron's resting potential by exchanging sodium and potassium ions across the membrane.", "tokens": [50668, 639, 5889, 33385, 264, 34090, 311, 21221, 3995, 538, 6210, 9741, 20265, 293, 29547, 27362, 2108, 264, 19651, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11137447907374455, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659397807597623e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 209808, "start": 2110.42, "end": 2111.2599999999998, "text": " Biological repair.", "tokens": [50982, 13007, 4383, 10535, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11137447907374455, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659397807597623e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 209808, "start": 2111.36, "end": 2115.94, "text": " If the cell runs out of ATP, if the energy supply fails, the pump stops.", "tokens": [51029, 759, 264, 2815, 6676, 484, 295, 39202, 11, 498, 264, 2281, 5847, 18199, 11, 264, 5889, 10094, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11137447907374455, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659397807597623e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 209808, "start": 2116.7799999999997, "end": 2119.94, "text": " The operator, the biological pump, structurally exists.", "tokens": [51300, 440, 12973, 11, 264, 13910, 5889, 11, 6594, 6512, 8198, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11137447907374455, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659397807597623e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 209808, "start": 2120.1, "end": 2125.56, "text": " It is sitting right there in the membrane, perfectly intact, but it energetically cannot execute.", "tokens": [51466, 467, 307, 3798, 558, 456, 294, 264, 19651, 11, 6239, 23493, 11, 457, 309, 2043, 847, 984, 2644, 14483, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11137447907374455, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659397807597623e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 212556, "start": 2125.56, "end": 2130.14, "text": " So to avoid that, systems build what the text calls a repair reserve.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 281, 5042, 300, 11, 3652, 1322, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 257, 10535, 17824, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 212556, "start": 2130.32, "end": 2130.64, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50603, 1079, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 212556, "start": 2130.84, "end": 2131.84, "text": " Like how humans walk.", "tokens": [50629, 1743, 577, 6255, 1792, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 212556, "start": 2132.18, "end": 2135.86, "text": " If I trip on a sidewalk, I don't rely on a single brain signal to catch me.", "tokens": [50696, 759, 286, 4931, 322, 257, 25360, 11, 286, 500, 380, 10687, 322, 257, 2167, 3567, 6358, 281, 3745, 385, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 212556, "start": 2136.16, "end": 2141.64, "text": " I have overlapping cellular oscillators, spinal cord reflexes, and muscle memory all firing at once.", "tokens": [50895, 286, 362, 33535, 29267, 18225, 3391, 11, 28022, 12250, 23802, 279, 11, 293, 8679, 4675, 439, 16045, 412, 1564, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 212556, "start": 2141.7599999999998, "end": 2143.16, "text": " The central pattern generators.", "tokens": [51175, 440, 5777, 5102, 38662, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 212556, "start": 2143.4, "end": 2145.54, "text": " You have overlapping substitutable pathways.", "tokens": [51257, 509, 362, 33535, 26441, 32148, 22988, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 212556, "start": 2145.7799999999997, "end": 2151.08, "text": " You only suffer a structural repair deficit when you exhaust the entire reserve across multiple layers of the system.", "tokens": [51376, 509, 787, 9753, 257, 15067, 10535, 22132, 562, 291, 14687, 264, 2302, 17824, 2108, 3866, 7914, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 212556, "start": 2151.2799999999997, "end": 2153.04, "text": " Biology is wildly resilient.", "tokens": [51651, 48132, 307, 34731, 23699, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 212556, "start": 2153.38, "end": 2153.7799999999997, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51756, 467, 307, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12573805932075746, "compression_ratio": 1.6258064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 215378, "start": 2153.78, "end": 2156.32, "text": " But even that can fail, which brings us to the final mode.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 754, 300, 393, 3061, 11, 597, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2572, 4391, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 215378, "start": 2156.78, "end": 2157.4, "text": " Mode 4.", "tokens": [50515, 20500, 1017, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 215378, "start": 2157.8, "end": 2158.76, "text": " Continuation failure.", "tokens": [50566, 14674, 16073, 7763, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 215378, "start": 2158.98, "end": 2160.34, "text": " This is composition failure.", "tokens": [50625, 639, 307, 12686, 7763, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 215378, "start": 2160.42, "end": 2160.5400000000004, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50697, 1779, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 215378, "start": 2160.6800000000003, "end": 2164.6200000000003, "text": " The local repair succeeds perfectly, but the global composition completely fails.", "tokens": [50710, 440, 2654, 10535, 49263, 6239, 11, 457, 264, 4338, 12686, 2584, 18199, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 215378, "start": 2164.98, "end": 2167.2000000000003, "text": " So the hospital's backup generators turn on.", "tokens": [50925, 407, 264, 4530, 311, 14807, 38662, 1261, 322, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 215378, "start": 2167.9, "end": 2169.6800000000003, "text": " Locally, they are functioning perfectly.", "tokens": [51071, 12859, 379, 11, 436, 366, 18483, 6239, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 215378, "start": 2169.96, "end": 2170.98, "text": " The engines are running.", "tokens": [51174, 440, 12982, 366, 2614, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 215378, "start": 2171.0800000000004, "end": 2172.1600000000003, "text": " The alternators are spinning.", "tokens": [51230, 440, 5400, 3391, 366, 15640, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19808553339360835, "compression_ratio": 1.6291079812206573, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555491565665604e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 217216, "start": 2172.16, "end": 2177.56, "text": " But they fail to synchronize their electrical phase with the hospital's internal grid.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 436, 3061, 281, 19331, 1125, 641, 12147, 5574, 365, 264, 4530, 311, 6920, 10748, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 217216, "start": 2178.3599999999997, "end": 2182.2599999999998, "text": " The power is being generated locally, but it can't be composed globally.", "tokens": [50675, 440, 1347, 307, 885, 10833, 16143, 11, 457, 309, 393, 380, 312, 18204, 18958, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 217216, "start": 2182.58, "end": 2185.54, "text": " The grid rejects it, and the hospital stays dark.", "tokens": [50886, 440, 10748, 8248, 82, 309, 11, 293, 264, 4530, 10834, 2877, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 217216, "start": 2185.68, "end": 2186.06, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51041, 3153, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 217216, "start": 2186.2799999999997, "end": 2190.14, "text": " And the cardiac synchronization example in the text mirrors this perfectly.", "tokens": [51071, 400, 264, 32129, 19331, 2144, 1365, 294, 264, 2487, 24238, 341, 6239, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 217216, "start": 2190.2599999999998, "end": 2190.68, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51270, 467, 775, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 217216, "start": 2191.06, "end": 2196.7799999999997, "text": " The human heartbeat is produced by a population of individual cellular oscillators in the heart tissue.", "tokens": [51310, 440, 1952, 34851, 307, 7126, 538, 257, 4415, 295, 2609, 29267, 18225, 3391, 294, 264, 1917, 12404, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13286469108179996, "compression_ratio": 1.6184738955823292, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813199053486438e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 219678, "start": 2196.78, "end": 2202.1400000000003, "text": " If the electrical coupling between those cells weakens, you get a lethal arrhythmia.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 12147, 37447, 1296, 729, 5438, 5336, 694, 11, 291, 483, 257, 34562, 5539, 34494, 654, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13305336778814142, "compression_ratio": 1.0632911392405062, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039887517152462e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 220214, "start": 2202.14, "end": 2204.2, "text": " Even though the individual cells are totally fine.", "tokens": [50365, 2754, 1673, 264, 2609, 5438, 366, 3879, 2489, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 220214, "start": 2204.2599999999998, "end": 2204.74, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50471, 7587, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 220214, "start": 2204.94, "end": 2209.54, "text": " If you look at any single cell locally under a microscope, it is functioning perfectly.", "tokens": [50505, 759, 291, 574, 412, 604, 2167, 2815, 16143, 833, 257, 29753, 11, 309, 307, 18483, 6239, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 220214, "start": 2209.72, "end": 2210.72, "text": " It is repairing itself.", "tokens": [50744, 467, 307, 46158, 2564, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 220214, "start": 2210.8199999999997, "end": 2211.74, "text": " It is oscillating.", "tokens": [50799, 467, 307, 18225, 990, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 220214, "start": 2211.9, "end": 2215.2, "text": " But they fail to glue together into a global rhythm.", "tokens": [50853, 583, 436, 3061, 281, 8998, 1214, 666, 257, 4338, 11801, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 220214, "start": 2215.44, "end": 2216.68, "text": " That is fascinating.", "tokens": [51030, 663, 307, 10343, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 220214, "start": 2216.8199999999997, "end": 2220.2599999999998, "text": " The local repairs are mathematically incompatible on the overlaps.", "tokens": [51099, 440, 2654, 28823, 366, 44003, 40393, 267, 964, 322, 264, 15986, 2382, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 220214, "start": 2220.3399999999997, "end": 2221.66, "text": " It is a continuation failure.", "tokens": [51275, 467, 307, 257, 29357, 7763, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17503618157428244, "compression_ratio": 1.6188340807174888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953990736671363e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 222166, "start": 2221.66, "end": 2225.48, "text": " So what does this all mean for how we define broken?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 577, 321, 6964, 5463, 30, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1479179922458345, "compression_ratio": 1.6327272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336678084071803e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 222166, "start": 2225.74, "end": 2231.48, "text": " Because if I look at the Posani et al. paper on cortical representations that Flixie mentioned,", "tokens": [50569, 1436, 498, 286, 574, 412, 264, 25906, 3782, 1030, 419, 13, 3035, 322, 11278, 804, 33358, 300, 3235, 970, 414, 2835, 11, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1479179922458345, "compression_ratio": 1.6327272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336678084071803e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 222166, "start": 2231.72, "end": 2236.68, "text": " if I look at a single neuron in the brain, it looks like a noisy, chaotic mess.", "tokens": [50868, 498, 286, 574, 412, 257, 2167, 34090, 294, 264, 3567, 11, 309, 1542, 411, 257, 24518, 11, 27013, 2082, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1479179922458345, "compression_ratio": 1.6327272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336678084071803e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 222166, "start": 2237.2799999999997, "end": 2238.74, "text": " It looks like diagnostic collapse.", "tokens": [51146, 467, 1542, 411, 27897, 15584, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1479179922458345, "compression_ratio": 1.6327272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336678084071803e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 222166, "start": 2239.08, "end": 2244.74, "text": " But if I zoom out and look at the whole population of neurons, the information is clearly there.", "tokens": [51236, 583, 498, 286, 8863, 484, 293, 574, 412, 264, 1379, 4415, 295, 22027, 11, 264, 1589, 307, 4448, 456, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1479179922458345, "compression_ratio": 1.6327272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336678084071803e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 222166, "start": 2245.42, "end": 2249.8599999999997, "text": " Doesn't this mean that failure is totally subjective based on how closely I'm squinting?", "tokens": [51553, 12955, 380, 341, 914, 300, 7763, 307, 3879, 25972, 2361, 322, 577, 8185, 286, 478, 2339, 686, 278, 30, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1479179922458345, "compression_ratio": 1.6327272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.1336678084071803e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 224986, "start": 2249.86, "end": 2255.7200000000003, "text": " I am so glad you brought that up because the text specifically praises the Posani paper for this exact insight.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 669, 370, 5404, 291, 3038, 300, 493, 570, 264, 2487, 4682, 3206, 3598, 264, 25906, 3782, 3035, 337, 341, 1900, 11269, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 224986, "start": 2256.32, "end": 2259.2400000000002, "text": " It calls it scale-dependent neural organization.", "tokens": [50688, 467, 5498, 309, 4373, 12, 36763, 317, 18161, 4475, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 224986, "start": 2260.1400000000003, "end": 2262.86, "text": " Restorability depends on separability, not categoricity.", "tokens": [50879, 13094, 284, 2310, 5946, 322, 3128, 2310, 11, 406, 4847, 16345, 507, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 224986, "start": 2263.6600000000003, "end": 2264.1600000000003, "text": " Break that down.", "tokens": [51055, 16925, 300, 760, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 224986, "start": 2264.32, "end": 2270.86, "text": " It means the brain doesn't need clean, perfectly labeled categories for every concept at the level of a single neuron.", "tokens": [51088, 467, 1355, 264, 3567, 1177, 380, 643, 2541, 11, 6239, 21335, 10479, 337, 633, 3410, 412, 264, 1496, 295, 257, 2167, 34090, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 224986, "start": 2271.2200000000003, "end": 2276.52, "text": " It just needs enough geometric structure at the massive population level to tell things apart.", "tokens": [51433, 467, 445, 2203, 1547, 33246, 3877, 412, 264, 5994, 4415, 1496, 281, 980, 721, 4936, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 224986, "start": 2276.7400000000002, "end": 2277.1, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51709, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13027185912525982, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7215941129286594e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 227710, "start": 2277.1, "end": 2284.08, "text": " A system can be completely unrestorable at a fine, zoomed-in scale because the local neurons look like pure noise,", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1185, 393, 312, 2584, 35103, 15249, 412, 257, 2489, 11, 8863, 292, 12, 259, 4373, 570, 264, 2654, 22027, 574, 411, 6075, 5658, 11, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 227710, "start": 2284.24, "end": 2287.7599999999998, "text": " but perfectly restorable at a coarse, zoomed-out scale, or vice versa.", "tokens": [50722, 457, 6239, 1472, 15249, 412, 257, 39312, 11, 8863, 292, 12, 346, 4373, 11, 420, 11964, 25650, 13, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 227710, "start": 2287.92, "end": 2288.64, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50906, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 227710, "start": 2288.7599999999998, "end": 2290.24, "text": " The boundary isn't a fixed wall.", "tokens": [50948, 440, 12866, 1943, 380, 257, 6806, 2929, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 227710, "start": 2290.36, "end": 2290.56, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51028, 865, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 227710, "start": 2290.72, "end": 2293.8199999999997, "text": " It's relative to the scale of the tools you're using to look at it.", "tokens": [51046, 467, 311, 4972, 281, 264, 4373, 295, 264, 3873, 291, 434, 1228, 281, 574, 412, 309, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 227710, "start": 2293.88, "end": 2294.3399999999997, "text": " However...", "tokens": [51204, 2908, 485, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 227710, "start": 2294.3399999999997, "end": 2295.22, "text": " I knew there was a however.", "tokens": [51227, 286, 2586, 456, 390, 257, 4461, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 227710, "start": 2295.3399999999997, "end": 2296.7999999999997, "text": " Look, there is a fixed wall.", "tokens": [51277, 2053, 11, 456, 307, 257, 6806, 2929, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 227710, "start": 2297.06, "end": 2300.46, "text": " There is an absolute limit that no change of scale can fix.", "tokens": [51363, 821, 307, 364, 8236, 4948, 300, 572, 1319, 295, 4373, 393, 3191, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11880625618828668, "compression_ratio": 1.6756756756756757, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 230046, "start": 2300.46, "end": 2303.7400000000002, "text": " Section six, reconstructive irreversibility.", "tokens": [50365, 21804, 2309, 11, 16891, 21673, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15396924086020025, "compression_ratio": 1.5194174757281553, "no_speech_prob": 1.483990773147592e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 230046, "start": 2304.96, "end": 2312.44, "text": " Because if all four of these repair modes fail, the alarms crash, the generators don't sink, the hospital goes totally dark.", "tokens": [50590, 1436, 498, 439, 1451, 295, 613, 10535, 14068, 3061, 11, 264, 45039, 8252, 11, 264, 38662, 500, 380, 9500, 11, 264, 4530, 1709, 3879, 2877, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15396924086020025, "compression_ratio": 1.5194174757281553, "no_speech_prob": 1.483990773147592e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 230046, "start": 2313.12, "end": 2319.9, "text": " Human intuition says, well, if we just had enough money or enough computing power, we could perfectly reconstruct what went wrong and hit undo.", "tokens": [50998, 10294, 24002, 1619, 11, 731, 11, 498, 321, 445, 632, 1547, 1460, 420, 1547, 15866, 1347, 11, 321, 727, 6239, 31499, 437, 1437, 2085, 293, 2045, 23779, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15396924086020025, "compression_ratio": 1.5194174757281553, "no_speech_prob": 1.483990773147592e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 231990, "start": 2319.9, "end": 2323.82, "text": " And the text gives a hard, mathematical, unequivocal no.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 2487, 2709, 257, 1152, 11, 18894, 11, 2251, 358, 592, 36483, 572, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 231990, "start": 2324.12, "end": 2324.52, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [50576, 1545, 30, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 231990, "start": 2325.0, "end": 2331.2200000000003, "text": " I mean, if I take a highly classified document and run it through a cross-cut shredder, I can theoretically tape it back together.", "tokens": [50620, 286, 914, 11, 498, 286, 747, 257, 5405, 20627, 4166, 293, 1190, 309, 807, 257, 3278, 12, 6672, 21567, 1068, 11, 286, 393, 29400, 7314, 309, 646, 1214, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 231990, "start": 2331.34, "end": 2331.7000000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50937, 1779, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 231990, "start": 2331.82, "end": 2337.0, "text": " It might take me a billion years in a supercomputer, but the information is physically still there in the shreds.", "tokens": [50961, 467, 1062, 747, 385, 257, 5218, 924, 294, 257, 36708, 11, 457, 264, 1589, 307, 9762, 920, 456, 294, 264, 21567, 82, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 231990, "start": 2337.2400000000002, "end": 2338.2000000000003, "text": " I can reconstruct it.", "tokens": [51232, 286, 393, 31499, 309, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 231990, "start": 2338.46, "end": 2343.0, "text": " That is true for a shredded document because shredding is just a complex rearrangement of matter.", "tokens": [51293, 663, 307, 2074, 337, 257, 39091, 4166, 570, 21567, 3584, 307, 445, 257, 3997, 39568, 518, 295, 1871, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10644643800752657, "compression_ratio": 1.6217228464419475, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691644590284161e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 234300, "start": 2343.0, "end": 2348.0, "text": " But the resource independence theorem addresses transitions that are fundamentally non-injective.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 7684, 14640, 20904, 16862, 23767, 300, 366, 17879, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 234300, "start": 2348.92, "end": 2353.48, "text": " Non-injective meaning multiple different paths collapsed into the exact same present state.", "tokens": [50661, 8774, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 3620, 3866, 819, 14518, 24578, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 1974, 1785, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 234300, "start": 2353.52, "end": 2353.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50891, 7587, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 234300, "start": 2354.04, "end": 2355.4, "text": " Let's use a mathematical analogy.", "tokens": [50917, 961, 311, 764, 257, 18894, 21663, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 234300, "start": 2355.64, "end": 2355.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50997, 1033, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 234300, "start": 2356.02, "end": 2361.44, "text": " If I hand you the number four and I ask you, did this come from two plus two or did it come from three plus one?", "tokens": [51016, 759, 286, 1011, 291, 264, 1230, 1451, 293, 286, 1029, 291, 11, 630, 341, 808, 490, 732, 1804, 732, 420, 630, 309, 808, 490, 1045, 1804, 472, 30, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 234300, "start": 2361.72, "end": 2362.94, "text": " I have absolutely no idea.", "tokens": [51301, 286, 362, 3122, 572, 1558, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 234300, "start": 2363.2, "end": 2367.98, "text": " And no amount of supercomputers in the universe can answer it because the input is fundamentally gone.", "tokens": [51375, 400, 572, 2372, 295, 27839, 2582, 433, 294, 264, 6445, 393, 1867, 309, 570, 264, 4846, 307, 17879, 2780, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12438016924364813, "compression_ratio": 1.6472602739726028, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236249541015657e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 236798, "start": 2367.98, "end": 2373.38, "text": " The distinction between two plus two and three plus one was destroyed in the operation of addition.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16844, 1296, 732, 1804, 732, 293, 1045, 1804, 472, 390, 8937, 294, 264, 6916, 295, 4500, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 236798, "start": 2373.84, "end": 2374.54, "text": " It evaporated.", "tokens": [50658, 467, 26315, 770, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 236798, "start": 2374.9, "end": 2384.6, "text": " The theorem states that if a fiber is subject to reconstructive irreversibility, no allocation of time, space, or energy will ever enable recovery.", "tokens": [50711, 440, 20904, 4368, 300, 498, 257, 12874, 307, 3983, 281, 16891, 21673, 16014, 840, 2841, 11, 572, 27599, 295, 565, 11, 1901, 11, 420, 2281, 486, 1562, 9528, 8597, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 236798, "start": 2385.18, "end": 2390.54, "text": " Because the domain element to compute from simply does not exist anymore in physical reality.", "tokens": [51225, 1436, 264, 9274, 4478, 281, 14722, 490, 2935, 775, 406, 2514, 3602, 294, 4001, 4103, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 236798, "start": 2390.64, "end": 2391.78, "text": " It's not a matter of budget.", "tokens": [51498, 467, 311, 406, 257, 1871, 295, 4706, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 236798, "start": 2392.2, "end": 2393.2400000000002, "text": " It's a matter of reality.", "tokens": [51576, 467, 311, 257, 1871, 295, 4103, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 236798, "start": 2393.36, "end": 2395.46, "text": " The information has evaporated.", "tokens": [51634, 440, 1589, 575, 26315, 770, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13708653222946893, "compression_ratio": 1.6654135338345866, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144626647189187e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 239546, "start": 2395.46, "end": 2402.3, "text": " This is a stark contrast with Hamiltonian dynamics in physics, where the flow of time is a diffeomorphism.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 257, 17417, 8712, 365, 18484, 952, 15679, 294, 10649, 11, 689, 264, 3095, 295, 565, 307, 257, 679, 2106, 32702, 1434, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 239546, "start": 2402.44, "end": 2404.18, "text": " You're going to have to explain diffeomorphism.", "tokens": [50714, 509, 434, 516, 281, 362, 281, 2903, 679, 2106, 32702, 1434, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 239546, "start": 2404.44, "end": 2410.1, "text": " In classical physics, every physical state maps perfectly to exactly one past state and one future state.", "tokens": [50814, 682, 13735, 10649, 11, 633, 4001, 1785, 11317, 6239, 281, 2293, 472, 1791, 1785, 293, 472, 2027, 1785, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 239546, "start": 2410.2, "end": 2411.08, "text": " Like a perfect chain.", "tokens": [51102, 1743, 257, 2176, 5021, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 239546, "start": 2411.2, "end": 2411.48, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51152, 1079, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 239546, "start": 2412.1, "end": 2421.94, "text": " If you know the exact position and momentum of every particle in a closed box, you can mathematically rewind the universe perfectly, even if it is infinitely expensive to compute.", "tokens": [51197, 759, 291, 458, 264, 1900, 2535, 293, 11244, 295, 633, 12359, 294, 257, 5395, 2424, 11, 291, 393, 44003, 41458, 264, 6445, 6239, 11, 754, 498, 309, 307, 36227, 5124, 281, 14722, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 239546, "start": 2422.08, "end": 2423.62, "text": " Like perfectly rewinding a video.", "tokens": [51696, 1743, 6239, 319, 86, 9245, 257, 960, 13, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10306046590083788, "compression_ratio": 1.7578947368421052, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450007548778354e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 242362, "start": 2423.62, "end": 2424.18, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18896495432093524, "compression_ratio": 1.515, "no_speech_prob": 1.890339230634086e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 242362, "start": 2424.74, "end": 2434.04, "text": " But in the systems we are talking about, biology, society, software fibers collapse, past states merge, things are forgotten.", "tokens": [50421, 583, 294, 264, 3652, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 11, 14956, 11, 4086, 11, 4722, 25252, 15584, 11, 1791, 4368, 22183, 11, 721, 366, 11832, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18896495432093524, "compression_ratio": 1.515, "no_speech_prob": 1.890339230634086e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 242362, "start": 2434.56, "end": 2438.2999999999997, "text": " Which leads to the distinction budget, denoted mathematically as BT.", "tokens": [50912, 3013, 6689, 281, 264, 16844, 4706, 11, 1441, 23325, 44003, 382, 31144, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18896495432093524, "compression_ratio": 1.515, "no_speech_prob": 1.890339230634086e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 242362, "start": 2439.02, "end": 2443.9, "text": " The text says, this is the set of collapsed fibers over which predecessor identity remains recoverable.", "tokens": [51135, 440, 2487, 1619, 11, 341, 307, 264, 992, 295, 24578, 25252, 670, 597, 34991, 6575, 7023, 8114, 712, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18896495432093524, "compression_ratio": 1.515, "no_speech_prob": 1.890339230634086e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 244390, "start": 2443.9, "end": 2445.7000000000003, "text": " And it has a terrifying property.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 575, 257, 18106, 4707, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 244390, "start": 2445.82, "end": 2446.58, "text": " It only shrinks.", "tokens": [50461, 467, 787, 9884, 16431, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 244390, "start": 2446.78, "end": 2447.48, "text": " It never grows.", "tokens": [50509, 467, 1128, 13156, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 244390, "start": 2447.78, "end": 2450.5, "text": " Once you lose the distinction, it is gone forever.", "tokens": [50559, 3443, 291, 3624, 264, 16844, 11, 309, 307, 2780, 5680, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 244390, "start": 2451.28, "end": 2457.1, "text": " This raises an incredibly important question about memory, data storage, and continuation in the modern world.", "tokens": [50734, 639, 19658, 364, 6252, 1021, 1168, 466, 4675, 11, 1412, 6725, 11, 293, 29357, 294, 264, 4363, 1002, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 244390, "start": 2457.5, "end": 2459.2400000000002, "text": " Because everyone just hoards data now.", "tokens": [51045, 1436, 1518, 445, 1106, 2287, 1412, 586, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 244390, "start": 2459.3, "end": 2459.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51135, 1779, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 244390, "start": 2459.78, "end": 2463.82, "text": " People assume that if you just have infinite cloud storage, you can reconstruct anything.", "tokens": [51159, 3432, 6552, 300, 498, 291, 445, 362, 13785, 4588, 6725, 11, 291, 393, 31499, 1340, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19040476481119792, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.958289867071139e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 246382, "start": 2463.82, "end": 2471.04, "text": " You hear companies say, just save all the data, but having infinite storage does not guarantee reconstruction if you chose to save the wrong thing.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1568, 3431, 584, 11, 445, 3155, 439, 264, 1412, 11, 457, 1419, 13785, 6725, 775, 406, 10815, 31565, 498, 291, 5111, 281, 3155, 264, 2085, 551, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08698912400465746, "compression_ratio": 1.5129533678756477, "no_speech_prob": 1.897744765153031e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 246382, "start": 2471.1000000000004, "end": 2479.26, "text": " Because injectivity, the ability to trace a result back to its unique cause, is a property of what is stored, not how much storage is available.", "tokens": [50729, 1436, 10711, 4253, 11, 264, 3485, 281, 13508, 257, 1874, 646, 281, 1080, 3845, 3082, 11, 307, 257, 4707, 295, 437, 307, 12187, 11, 406, 577, 709, 6725, 307, 2435, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08698912400465746, "compression_ratio": 1.5129533678756477, "no_speech_prob": 1.897744765153031e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 247926, "start": 2479.26, "end": 2479.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 247926, "start": 2480.0, "end": 2481.32, "text": " So you shouldn't just save everything.", "tokens": [50402, 407, 291, 4659, 380, 445, 3155, 1203, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 247926, "start": 2481.82, "end": 2484.8, "text": " The text calls this admissibility-aware externalization.", "tokens": [50493, 440, 2487, 5498, 341, 5910, 891, 2841, 12, 17074, 8320, 2144, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 247926, "start": 2485.0800000000004, "end": 2485.26, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50656, 1033, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 247926, "start": 2485.48, "end": 2490.8, "text": " Over-retention wastes resources and creates diagnostic collapse by drowning you in noise.", "tokens": [50676, 4886, 12, 1505, 1251, 390, 7269, 3593, 293, 7829, 27897, 15584, 538, 37198, 291, 294, 5658, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 247926, "start": 2491.26, "end": 2498.4, "text": " You should only allocate history channels to admissibility-relevant fibers, and you rank them by relevance per unit cost.", "tokens": [50965, 509, 820, 787, 35713, 2503, 9235, 281, 5910, 891, 2841, 12, 265, 25638, 25252, 11, 293, 291, 6181, 552, 538, 32684, 680, 4985, 2063, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 247926, "start": 2498.5200000000004, "end": 2500.2000000000003, "text": " So you don't just back up the whole hard drive.", "tokens": [51328, 407, 291, 500, 380, 445, 646, 493, 264, 1379, 1152, 3332, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 247926, "start": 2500.34, "end": 2506.1400000000003, "text": " You selectively back up the exact decisions that your future rules will need to judge.", "tokens": [51419, 509, 3048, 3413, 646, 493, 264, 1900, 5327, 300, 428, 2027, 4474, 486, 643, 281, 6995, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 247926, "start": 2506.2200000000003, "end": 2506.6800000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51713, 7587, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1785680656759148, "compression_ratio": 1.6583629893238434, "no_speech_prob": 2.1423464131170578e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 250668, "start": 2506.68, "end": 2508.3599999999997, "text": " It's an exquisite design principle.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 364, 454, 34152, 1715, 8665, 13, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 250668, "start": 2508.8599999999997, "end": 2513.72, "text": " Save exactly what the future constraint network will need to evaluate, and let the rest collapse.", "tokens": [50474, 15541, 2293, 437, 264, 2027, 25534, 3209, 486, 643, 281, 13059, 11, 293, 718, 264, 1472, 15584, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 250668, "start": 2514.0, "end": 2520.24, "text": " To ensure we truly grasp how all these highly abstract concepts map onto physical reality, let's bring it all together.", "tokens": [50731, 1407, 5586, 321, 4908, 21743, 577, 439, 613, 5405, 12649, 10392, 4471, 3911, 4001, 4103, 11, 718, 311, 1565, 309, 439, 1214, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 250668, "start": 2520.3399999999997, "end": 2520.7999999999997, "text": " Let's do it.", "tokens": [51048, 961, 311, 360, 309, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 250668, "start": 2520.7999999999997, "end": 2528.12, "text": " The text synthesizes the entire framework using a brilliant, multi-layered, real-world example in Appendix E.", "tokens": [51071, 440, 2487, 26617, 5660, 264, 2302, 8388, 1228, 257, 10248, 11, 4825, 12, 8376, 4073, 11, 957, 12, 13217, 1365, 294, 3132, 521, 970, 462, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 250668, "start": 2528.52, "end": 2531.3999999999996, "text": " It's a four-tier autonomous vehicle highway.", "tokens": [51457, 467, 311, 257, 1451, 12, 25402, 23797, 5864, 17205, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 250668, "start": 2531.58, "end": 2535.04, "text": " Let's walk through this tier by tier, because it demonstrates everything we've discussed.", "tokens": [51610, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 341, 12362, 538, 12362, 11, 570, 309, 31034, 1203, 321, 600, 7152, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 250668, "start": 2535.16, "end": 2535.8999999999996, "text": " I love this section.", "tokens": [51789, 286, 959, 341, 3541, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271673349233774, "compression_ratio": 1.592814371257485, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431003913893293e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 253590, "start": 2535.9, "end": 2538.44, "text": " Okay, tier one is digmergic control.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 12362, 472, 307, 2528, 936, 11577, 1969, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13590613655422046, "compression_ratio": 1.5274261603375527, "no_speech_prob": 1.472219156480048e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 253590, "start": 2539.28, "end": 2546.32, "text": " The autonomous vehicles are driving at 80 miles an hour, but they aren't talking to a central server to get their absolute GPS coordinates.", "tokens": [50534, 440, 23797, 8948, 366, 4840, 412, 4688, 6193, 364, 1773, 11, 457, 436, 3212, 380, 1417, 281, 257, 5777, 7154, 281, 483, 641, 8236, 19462, 21056, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13590613655422046, "compression_ratio": 1.5274261603375527, "no_speech_prob": 1.472219156480048e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 253590, "start": 2546.56, "end": 2550.7400000000002, "text": " They are just tracking the gap in the closing rate to the car immediately in front of them.", "tokens": [50898, 814, 366, 445, 11603, 264, 7417, 294, 264, 10377, 3314, 281, 264, 1032, 4258, 294, 1868, 295, 552, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13590613655422046, "compression_ratio": 1.5274261603375527, "no_speech_prob": 1.472219156480048e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 253590, "start": 2550.94, "end": 2555.7200000000003, "text": " Like ants following a pheromone trail, or a flock of starlings maneuvering in the sky.", "tokens": [51117, 1743, 23355, 3480, 257, 280, 511, 298, 546, 9924, 11, 420, 257, 34819, 295, 3543, 20823, 25976, 278, 294, 264, 5443, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13590613655422046, "compression_ratio": 1.5274261603375527, "no_speech_prob": 1.472219156480048e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 253590, "start": 2555.84, "end": 2556.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51362, 1779, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13590613655422046, "compression_ratio": 1.5274261603375527, "no_speech_prob": 1.472219156480048e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 255606, "start": 2556.06, "end": 2558.74, "text": " This demonstrates pairwise admissibility.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 31034, 6119, 3711, 5910, 891, 2841, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18627569752354775, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617352025655174e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 255606, "start": 2558.74, "end": 2563.24, "text": " It also beautifully demonstrates separability over categoricity.", "tokens": [50499, 467, 611, 16525, 31034, 3128, 2310, 670, 4847, 16345, 507, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18627569752354775, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617352025655174e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 255606, "start": 2563.98, "end": 2569.34, "text": " The car's computer doesn't need to categorize the situation as moderate traffic condition 4B with light rain.", "tokens": [50761, 440, 1032, 311, 3820, 1177, 380, 643, 281, 19250, 1125, 264, 2590, 382, 18174, 6419, 4188, 1017, 33, 365, 1442, 4830, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18627569752354775, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617352025655174e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 255606, "start": 2569.52, "end": 2572.62, "text": " It just needs to separate safe gap from unsafe gap.", "tokens": [51038, 467, 445, 2203, 281, 4994, 3273, 7417, 490, 35948, 7417, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18627569752354775, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617352025655174e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 257262, "start": 2572.62, "end": 2574.3399999999997, "text": " It's acting purely on distinctions.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 6577, 17491, 322, 1483, 49798, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 257262, "start": 2574.48, "end": 2574.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50458, 1079, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 257262, "start": 2574.92, "end": 2575.8399999999997, "text": " Okay, tier two.", "tokens": [50480, 1033, 11, 12362, 732, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 257262, "start": 2576.46, "end": 2577.6, "text": " Diagnostic escalation.", "tokens": [50557, 8789, 4535, 19634, 17871, 399, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 257262, "start": 2578.54, "end": 2583.64, "text": " The car's camera gets confused by a weirdly shaped flatbed truck carrying a reflective mirror.", "tokens": [50661, 440, 1032, 311, 2799, 2170, 9019, 538, 257, 48931, 13475, 4962, 2883, 5898, 9792, 257, 28931, 8013, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 257262, "start": 2584.0, "end": 2585.46, "text": " It hits diagnostic collapse.", "tokens": [50934, 467, 8664, 27897, 15584, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 257262, "start": 2585.94, "end": 2590.46, "text": " The signal is there, but there is zero mutual information about what the object actually is.", "tokens": [51031, 440, 6358, 307, 456, 11, 457, 456, 307, 4018, 16917, 1589, 466, 437, 264, 2657, 767, 307, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 257262, "start": 2590.54, "end": 2595.8599999999997, "text": " Now, instead of just staring harder at the truck and eventually crashing, it routes the camera feed to the passenger's tablet.", "tokens": [51261, 823, 11, 2602, 295, 445, 18043, 6081, 412, 264, 5898, 293, 4728, 26900, 11, 309, 18242, 264, 2799, 3154, 281, 264, 18707, 311, 14136, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 257262, "start": 2596.16, "end": 2598.24, "text": " It asks the human, hey, what is this?", "tokens": [51542, 467, 8962, 264, 1952, 11, 4177, 11, 437, 307, 341, 30, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1701386015293962, "compression_ratio": 1.6232394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 3.970987167561946e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 259824, "start": 2598.24, "end": 2600.8799999999997, "text": " It opens a new diagnostic channel by passing the collapse.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 9870, 257, 777, 27897, 2269, 538, 8437, 264, 15584, 13, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 259824, "start": 2601.06, "end": 2601.5, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50506, 7587, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 259824, "start": 2601.72, "end": 2602.3999999999996, "text": " But it goes further.", "tokens": [50539, 583, 309, 1709, 3052, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 259824, "start": 2602.72, "end": 2608.52, "text": " Let's say the passenger uses the tablet to take control of a local drone to scout ahead, and they notice debris on the road.", "tokens": [50589, 961, 311, 584, 264, 18707, 4960, 264, 14136, 281, 747, 1969, 295, 257, 2654, 13852, 281, 34392, 2286, 11, 293, 436, 3449, 21942, 322, 264, 3060, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 259824, "start": 2609.06, "end": 2614.18, "text": " The passenger manually alters the coordination geometry for the other cars in the lane to route around it.", "tokens": [50906, 440, 18707, 16945, 419, 1559, 264, 21252, 18426, 337, 264, 661, 5163, 294, 264, 12705, 281, 7955, 926, 309, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 259824, "start": 2614.62, "end": 2617.2999999999997, "text": " This is level three geometric repair.", "tokens": [51184, 639, 307, 1496, 1045, 33246, 10535, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 259824, "start": 2617.2999999999997, "end": 2619.3199999999997, "text": " They aren't just moving their own car.", "tokens": [51318, 814, 3212, 380, 445, 2684, 641, 1065, 1032, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 259824, "start": 2619.54, "end": 2622.5, "text": " They are authoring the rules of the geometry itself.", "tokens": [51430, 814, 366, 3793, 278, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 18426, 2564, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 259824, "start": 2622.8199999999997, "end": 2626.5, "text": " And this is where I had a massive aha moment, because this layers so beautifully.", "tokens": [51594, 400, 341, 307, 689, 286, 632, 257, 5994, 47340, 1623, 11, 570, 341, 7914, 370, 16525, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15816372124723685, "compression_ratio": 1.694267515923567, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214437340873356e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 262650, "start": 2626.5, "end": 2630.16, "text": " Tier one is just checking the rules of the gap safe.", "tokens": [50365, 24224, 472, 307, 445, 8568, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 7417, 3273, 13, 50548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 262650, "start": 2631.1, "end": 2635.16, "text": " But tier two is actively rewriting the rules based on new information.", "tokens": [50595, 583, 12362, 732, 307, 13022, 319, 19868, 264, 4474, 2361, 322, 777, 1589, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 262650, "start": 2635.9, "end": 2637.6, "text": " Checking versus authoring.", "tokens": [50835, 6881, 278, 5717, 3793, 278, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 262650, "start": 2637.9, "end": 2643.52, "text": " And you have hit on exactly how this example resolves a major theoretical conflict in the source text.", "tokens": [50935, 400, 291, 362, 2045, 322, 2293, 577, 341, 1365, 7923, 977, 257, 2563, 20864, 6596, 294, 264, 4009, 2487, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 262650, "start": 2643.78, "end": 2644.04, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51229, 4083, 30, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 262650, "start": 2644.28, "end": 2644.58, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51254, 1079, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 262650, "start": 2645.18, "end": 2650.34, "text": " Some theorists in the field argue that admissibility is a fixed, objective rule you check against.", "tokens": [51299, 2188, 27423, 1751, 294, 264, 2519, 9695, 300, 5910, 891, 2841, 307, 257, 6806, 11, 10024, 4978, 291, 1520, 1970, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 262650, "start": 2650.96, "end": 2653.62, "text": " Others argue it is something a system authors dynamically.", "tokens": [51588, 20277, 9695, 309, 307, 746, 257, 1185, 16552, 43492, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820313226609003, "compression_ratio": 1.6121673003802282, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947558807711705e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 265362, "start": 2653.62, "end": 2656.7799999999997, "text": " The highway example proves they aren't competing theories.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 17205, 1365, 25019, 436, 3212, 380, 15439, 13667, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 265362, "start": 2656.94, "end": 2659.16, "text": " It just happened at different levels of the exact same system.", "tokens": [50531, 467, 445, 2011, 412, 819, 4358, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 1185, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 265362, "start": 2659.2599999999998, "end": 2659.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50647, 1079, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 265362, "start": 2659.88, "end": 2661.56, "text": " The car's camera checks the geometry.", "tokens": [50678, 440, 1032, 311, 2799, 13834, 264, 18426, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 265362, "start": 2661.8199999999997, "end": 2662.96, "text": " The passenger authors it.", "tokens": [50775, 440, 18707, 16552, 309, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 265362, "start": 2663.06, "end": 2663.7799999999997, "text": " Okay, tier three.", "tokens": [50837, 1033, 11, 12362, 1045, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 265362, "start": 2664.52, "end": 2665.48, "text": " The salience screen.", "tokens": [50910, 440, 1845, 1182, 2568, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 265362, "start": 2666.48, "end": 2669.7, "text": " Because the car shouldn't bug the human for every single shadow on the road.", "tokens": [51008, 1436, 264, 1032, 4659, 380, 7426, 264, 1952, 337, 633, 2167, 8576, 322, 264, 3060, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 265362, "start": 2670.58, "end": 2673.9, "text": " The central console ranks pending questions by relevance per unit cost.", "tokens": [51213, 440, 5777, 11076, 21406, 32110, 1651, 538, 32684, 680, 4985, 2063, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 265362, "start": 2674.3199999999997, "end": 2676.62, "text": " This is admissibility-aware externalization.", "tokens": [51400, 639, 307, 5910, 891, 2841, 12, 17074, 8320, 2144, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16474091003988392, "compression_ratio": 1.5437956204379562, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308570383565367e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 267662, "start": 2676.62, "end": 2682.8399999999997, "text": " It only asks for human attention, which has a very high computational cost, for fibers that are highly relevant to safety.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 787, 8962, 337, 1952, 3202, 11, 597, 575, 257, 588, 1090, 28270, 2063, 11, 337, 25252, 300, 366, 5405, 7340, 281, 4514, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 267662, "start": 2683.2599999999998, "end": 2684.64, "text": " Selective retention at work.", "tokens": [50697, 13638, 488, 22871, 412, 589, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 267662, "start": 2685.2599999999998, "end": 2688.48, "text": " It manages its distinction budget flawlessly.", "tokens": [50797, 467, 22489, 1080, 16844, 4706, 13717, 12048, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 267662, "start": 2688.8599999999997, "end": 2690.14, "text": " And finally, tier four.", "tokens": [50977, 400, 2721, 11, 12362, 1451, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 267662, "start": 2690.94, "end": 2691.74, "text": " Tower pilots.", "tokens": [51081, 17877, 21506, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 267662, "start": 2692.2599999999998, "end": 2697.72, "text": " Human air traffic controllers for the highway, invoked only for massive accidents or extreme ambiguity.", "tokens": [51147, 10294, 1988, 6419, 26903, 337, 264, 17205, 11, 1048, 9511, 787, 337, 5994, 23875, 420, 8084, 46519, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 267662, "start": 2698.2, "end": 2699.54, "text": " This is the architecture gate.", "tokens": [51444, 639, 307, 264, 9482, 8539, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020288664719154, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.6768201370763745e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 269954, "start": 2699.54, "end": 2711.56, "text": " The tower pilots deal with the ontological boundaries, the situations that the car's architecture fundamentally cannot represent, like a sinkhole opening up or a plane landing on the interstate.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10567, 21506, 2028, 365, 264, 6592, 4383, 13180, 11, 264, 6851, 300, 264, 1032, 311, 9482, 17879, 2644, 2906, 11, 411, 257, 9500, 14094, 5193, 493, 420, 257, 5720, 11202, 322, 264, 728, 15406, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058239813645680746, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343071423425727e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 269954, "start": 2711.7, "end": 2715.92, "text": " And notice, they are invoked very rarely, but they are a keystone operator.", "tokens": [50973, 400, 3449, 11, 436, 366, 1048, 9511, 588, 13752, 11, 457, 436, 366, 257, 2141, 11243, 12973, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058239813645680746, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343071423425727e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 271592, "start": 2715.92, "end": 2726.5, "text": " Yes, their laws would disconnect massive future state spaces, because without them, any out-of-architecture anomaly would permanently paralyze the entire highway network.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 641, 6064, 576, 14299, 5994, 2027, 1785, 7673, 11, 570, 1553, 552, 11, 604, 484, 12, 2670, 12, 1178, 5739, 540, 42737, 576, 24042, 32645, 1381, 264, 2302, 17205, 3209, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07797986558340128, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507266453890672e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 271592, "start": 2726.6, "end": 2730.58, "text": " It is the entire mathematical framework, perfectly realized on a stretch of asphalt.", "tokens": [50899, 467, 307, 264, 2302, 18894, 8388, 11, 6239, 5334, 322, 257, 5985, 295, 46076, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07797986558340128, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507266453890672e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 271592, "start": 2730.78, "end": 2731.52, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51108, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07797986558340128, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507266453890672e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 271592, "start": 2731.56, "end": 2743.04, "text": " We have been on an incredible journey today, from the mathematical bedrock of distinctions and blind spots, to the masking pathology of constraints where diversity lies to you, to the shrinking future of entropy.", "tokens": [51147, 492, 362, 668, 322, 364, 4651, 4671, 965, 11, 490, 264, 18894, 2901, 17799, 295, 1483, 49798, 293, 6865, 10681, 11, 281, 264, 31226, 3100, 1793, 295, 18491, 689, 8811, 9134, 281, 291, 11, 281, 264, 41684, 2027, 295, 30867, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07797986558340128, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507266453890672e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 274304, "start": 2743.04, "end": 2757.3, "text": " We explored the anti-alignment of striving for efficiency over repairability, the four distinct failure boundaries of the hospital power grid, and finally, the absolute hard wall of reconstructive irreversibility.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 24016, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 295, 36582, 337, 10493, 670, 10535, 2310, 11, 264, 1451, 10644, 7763, 13180, 295, 264, 4530, 1347, 10748, 11, 293, 2721, 11, 264, 8236, 1152, 2929, 295, 16891, 21673, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161287443978446, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 2.150745727347303e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 274304, "start": 2757.48, "end": 2763.24, "text": " And the takeaway here for you, the listener, is that persistence isn't just a static fact.", "tokens": [51087, 400, 264, 30681, 510, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 307, 300, 37617, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 13437, 1186, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161287443978446, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 2.150745727347303e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 274304, "start": 2763.62, "end": 2764.98, "text": " It isn't just something that is.", "tokens": [51394, 467, 1943, 380, 445, 746, 300, 307, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161287443978446, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 2.150745727347303e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 274304, "start": 2765.08, "end": 2765.7799999999997, "text": " No, it's not.", "tokens": [51467, 883, 11, 309, 311, 406, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161287443978446, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 2.150745727347303e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 276578, "start": 2765.78, "end": 2778.78, "text": " Whether it's the cells beating in your heart, the software running your bank, or the institutions governing your society, structures only exist because a hidden, deeply layered ecology of repair is constantly fighting off entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 8503, 309, 311, 264, 5438, 13497, 294, 428, 1917, 11, 264, 4722, 2614, 428, 3765, 11, 420, 264, 8142, 30054, 428, 4086, 11, 9227, 787, 2514, 570, 257, 7633, 11, 8760, 34666, 39683, 295, 10535, 307, 6460, 5237, 766, 30867, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08986733436584472, "compression_ratio": 1.5985915492957747, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396462738573538e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 276578, "start": 2779.34, "end": 2783.88, "text": " The moment that ecology fails, the structure is already a ghost.", "tokens": [51043, 440, 1623, 300, 39683, 18199, 11, 264, 3877, 307, 1217, 257, 8359, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08986733436584472, "compression_ratio": 1.5985915492957747, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396462738573538e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 276578, "start": 2784.3, "end": 2785.5800000000004, "text": " It just hasn't fallen down yet.", "tokens": [51291, 467, 445, 6132, 380, 11547, 760, 1939, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08986733436584472, "compression_ratio": 1.5985915492957747, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396462738573538e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 276578, "start": 2785.7400000000002, "end": 2791.0800000000004, "text": " And I will leave you with a final thought, built directly on the source material's repair-recovery separation principle.", "tokens": [51363, 400, 286, 486, 1856, 291, 365, 257, 2572, 1194, 11, 3094, 3838, 322, 264, 4009, 2527, 311, 10535, 12, 265, 21352, 14634, 8665, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08986733436584472, "compression_ratio": 1.5985915492957747, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396462738573538e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 276578, "start": 2791.2000000000003, "end": 2791.42, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51636, 1033, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08986733436584472, "compression_ratio": 1.5985915492957747, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396462738573538e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 279142, "start": 2791.42, "end": 2802.34, "text": " When one of these ecologies successfully repairs a system so it works again, when the hospital power comes back on, or the piano is retuned, it does not mean the historical identity of what went wrong has been preserved.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 472, 295, 613, 11437, 6204, 10727, 28823, 257, 1185, 370, 309, 1985, 797, 11, 562, 264, 4530, 1347, 1487, 646, 322, 11, 420, 264, 9211, 307, 1533, 43703, 11, 309, 775, 406, 914, 264, 8584, 6575, 295, 437, 1437, 2085, 575, 668, 22242, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09131637128811439, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043322269634896e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 279142, "start": 2802.8, "end": 2812.5, "text": " We are constantly fixing our systems, our code, our laws, our own biological bodies, in ways that silently, permanently erase the evidence of the original faults.", "tokens": [50934, 492, 366, 6460, 19442, 527, 3652, 11, 527, 3089, 11, 527, 6064, 11, 527, 1065, 13910, 7510, 11, 294, 2098, 300, 40087, 11, 24042, 23525, 264, 4467, 295, 264, 3380, 36090, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09131637128811439, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043322269634896e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 279142, "start": 2813.12, "end": 2818.3, "text": " A minimality-driven repair patches the whole, but it destroys the forensic trace forever.", "tokens": [51450, 316, 4464, 1860, 12, 25456, 10535, 26531, 264, 1379, 11, 457, 309, 36714, 264, 39084, 13508, 5680, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09131637128811439, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043322269634896e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 281830, "start": 2818.3, "end": 2829.3, "text": " So ask yourself, how much of your current life, how much of our current civilization is running flawlessly right now, while completely built on an empty distinction budget that can never, ever be reconstructed?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1029, 1803, 11, 577, 709, 295, 428, 2190, 993, 11, 577, 709, 295, 527, 2190, 18036, 307, 2614, 13717, 12048, 558, 586, 11, 1339, 2584, 3094, 322, 364, 6707, 16844, 4706, 300, 393, 1128, 11, 1562, 312, 31499, 292, 30, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0958215549427976, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496139748645942e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 281830, "start": 2830.3, "end": 2830.98, "text": " Sobering thought.", "tokens": [50965, 407, 607, 278, 1194, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0958215549427976, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496139748645942e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 281830, "start": 2831.2000000000003, "end": 2832.48, "text": " That is going to keep me up at night.", "tokens": [51010, 663, 307, 516, 281, 1066, 385, 493, 412, 1818, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0958215549427976, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496139748645942e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 281830, "start": 2832.7400000000002, "end": 2834.5, "text": " Thank you so much for joining us on this deep dive.", "tokens": [51087, 1044, 291, 370, 709, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0958215549427976, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496139748645942e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 281830, "start": 2835.0, "end": 2837.78, "text": " Keep wondering, keep learning, and we will see you next time.", "tokens": [51200, 5527, 6359, 11, 1066, 2539, 11, 293, 321, 486, 536, 291, 958, 565, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0958215549427976, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496139748645942e-12}], "language": "en"}
